WEBVTT


00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.300
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:50.902 --> 00:00:52.907
[crowd chanting]
Pink Slip! Pink Slip!


00:00:53.042 --> 00:00:55.415
Pink Slip! Pink Slip!


00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:56.909
Pink Slip! Pink Slip!


00:00:57.044 --> 00:00:58.984
[guitar playing]


00:01:14.997 --> 00:01:16.392
[phone chimes]


00:01:16.528 --> 00:01:17.994
[Siri] <i>Text from Mom:</i>


00:01:18.129 --> 00:01:19.822
<i>"Hi, honey. I noticed
you haven't chimed in</i>


00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:21.337
<i>on the family chat."</i>


00:01:21.472 --> 00:01:23.120
<i>Text from Mom: "Maybe
we can all FaceTime?"</i>


00:01:23.203 --> 00:01:24.603
<i>Text from Mom:</i>


00:01:24.739 --> 00:01:25.895
<i>"I'm just about to
record a new episode."</i>


00:01:25.978 --> 00:01:27.006
[♪ "Rebel Rebel" playing]


00:01:27.141 --> 00:01:28.514
Hi. Welcome back.


00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:30.180
I'm Dr. Tess Coleman,


00:01:30.316 --> 00:01:32.947
and this is <i>Rebelling
with Respect</i>.


00:01:33.082 --> 00:01:34.811
Today on the podcast,


00:01:34.946 --> 00:01:37.383
we are talking about
a relationship dynamic


00:01:37.518 --> 00:01:39.789
that is very close to my heart.


00:01:39.924 --> 00:01:42.160
"Grand co-parenting."


00:01:42.296 --> 00:01:45.257
When my daughter, Anna,
chose to become a single mom,


00:01:45.393 --> 00:01:46.993
it changed our family forever.


00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:48.798
[mechanical buzzing]


00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:51.230
Ryan! Cloffice. Recording.


00:01:51.365 --> 00:01:53.129
[Ryan clears throat, spits]


00:01:53.264 --> 00:01:54.906
Sorry!


00:01:55.375 --> 00:01:59.741
As a grandma, I was able
to step up and help her.


00:01:59.876 --> 00:02:01.343
[alarm ringing]


00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:06.583
[Anna] Harper! [breathes deeply]


00:02:07.252 --> 00:02:09.149
Harper, this is your
30-minute warning


00:02:09.285 --> 00:02:11.188
that we're leaving for school.


00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.392
Harp?


00:02:13.995 --> 00:02:15.786
This is now your
20-minute warning.


00:02:16.387 --> 00:02:17.390
Ten minutes.


00:02:17.526 --> 00:02:19.298
Yes, confirm the
recording sessions.


00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:22.000
But know that I know she can
sell out more than the Greek.


00:02:22.136 --> 00:02:23.765
And yes, I know how
many seats there are.


00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.335
[knocks on door]


00:02:25.471 --> 00:02:27.016
[Anna] Harper! I really
wanna respect your space,


00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:29.102
but I'm curious as to why
you're not out here yet.


00:02:29.237 --> 00:02:30.738
You have five minutes!


00:02:30.873 --> 00:02:33.210
[Tess] <i>Being someone that
your loved one can lean on</i>


00:02:33.346 --> 00:02:36.774
is the most important
relationship there is.


00:02:39.988 --> 00:02:42.950
Ryan, I'm getting
so good at this!


00:02:43.085 --> 00:02:45.189
[computer chimes]


00:02:45.591 --> 00:02:46.960
No.


00:02:48.419 --> 00:02:49.485
No, no, no!


00:02:49.921 --> 00:02:52.059
-Oh, it didn't record!
-[beeping]


00:02:52.194 --> 00:02:53.798
-Moth...
-[beeping]


00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.065
-[phone ringing]
-Hi, Mom.


00:02:55.201 --> 00:02:56.697
Now is not a great
time. I'm just...


00:02:56.833 --> 00:02:58.352
[Tess] <i>I know, but I
finished my podcast early,</i>


00:02:58.435 --> 00:03:00.205
<i>so I'm offering to do drop-off.</i>


00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.905
No. It's okay. I've got
everything under control.


00:03:03.308 --> 00:03:05.005
Harper, you had to be
up ten minutes ago!


00:03:05.141 --> 00:03:06.469
Prepare to be triggered!


00:03:06.605 --> 00:03:07.904
[♪ "HOT TO GO!" playing]


00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.185
Harper!


00:03:26.629 --> 00:03:28.428
-Let's catch one more.
-[surfers chuckling]


00:03:28.563 --> 00:03:30.530
[surfer] Dude, these
waves are unreal.


00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:33.004
[Harper] I love our
lives! [chuckling]


00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.936
Yo, are we skipping
first period?


00:03:35.072 --> 00:03:36.900
Oh, shoot. We gotta go.


00:03:44.951 --> 00:03:46.217
-Harper!
-[Harper] What?


00:03:46.886 --> 00:03:47.981
I'm literally ready.


00:03:48.116 --> 00:03:49.755
Barely. Barely.


00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:51.615
I made your favorite lunch.


00:03:52.117 --> 00:03:54.256
How was pickleball
yesterday? Did you beat 'em?


00:03:54.392 --> 00:03:57.292
-We say "annihilated."
-[chuckling]


00:03:57.427 --> 00:03:59.488
Mom, I told you
I could take her.


00:03:59.624 --> 00:04:00.556
I know, sweetheart.


00:04:00.692 --> 00:04:02.024
But I saw on your stories


00:04:02.159 --> 00:04:03.835
that you were working
at the studio late,


00:04:03.971 --> 00:04:05.468
and so I decided to take her.


00:04:05.604 --> 00:04:07.655
You know, it would be healthy
for you to unfollow me.


00:04:07.738 --> 00:04:09.973
And I work late all the
time. I can still take her.


00:04:10.109 --> 00:04:12.440
Anna, let's pause and reframe.


00:04:12.575 --> 00:04:14.477
When you decided
to be a single mom,


00:04:14.612 --> 00:04:16.578
I told you I would support
you a hundred percent.


00:04:16.713 --> 00:04:19.442
Well, this is me supporting
you a hundred percent.


00:04:19.578 --> 00:04:20.882
Okay, you know what?


00:04:21.017 --> 00:04:22.251
I'm coming too.


00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:23.827
We can both do
drop-off this morning.


00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:26.049
-[Anna] Mom.
-No, go on. You can go.


00:04:26.184 --> 00:04:27.875
-[Anna] Just let them...
-Oh, okay, you're not going.


00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:29.027
[horns honking]


00:04:29.162 --> 00:04:30.322
-[Anna] Mom.
-You're gonna go.


00:04:30.428 --> 00:04:31.682
You're not... Nobody's gonna go.


00:04:31.765 --> 00:04:32.993
I'm gonna go!


00:04:33.696 --> 00:04:35.993
-So what's up, kiddo?
-[Harper] Nothing.


00:04:36.696 --> 00:04:38.071
-Okay, spill it.
-All right.


00:04:38.206 --> 00:04:40.338
My new lab partner is
the absolute worst.


00:04:40.473 --> 00:04:42.465
<i>She's the new girl,
here for the year.</i>


00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.834
<i>I mean, ugh,</i>


00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:45.308
<i>she thinks she's so much better</i>


00:04:45.443 --> 00:04:47.444
<i>than everyone because
she's British,</i>


00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.347
which she has to remind
you of every five seconds.


00:04:50.482 --> 00:04:52.451
Like no one's ever been
from England before.


00:04:52.587 --> 00:04:54.832
[lab partner] So my dad opened
his third restaurant in Paris,


00:04:54.915 --> 00:04:56.621
and that's how I met
my French boyfriend,


00:04:56.756 --> 00:04:57.880
Philippe Henri.


00:04:58.016 --> 00:05:00.483
-[sighs] Philippe Henri.
-Ooh, la-la.


00:05:00.619 --> 00:05:01.952
He's French and a model.


00:05:02.088 --> 00:05:03.895
You've seriously been
to Paris Fashion Week?


00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:05.228
Anna Wintour scowled at me.


00:05:05.364 --> 00:05:07.164
-Seriously?
-What's Paris like?


00:05:07.299 --> 00:05:09.393
Oh, it's lovely.
I go all the time.


00:05:09.529 --> 00:05:11.127
Ignore the British girl.


00:05:11.262 --> 00:05:14.004
After this year, you won't
have to see her anymore.


00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.900
Nice advice from a therapist.


00:05:16.035 --> 00:05:17.969
Well, I'm not her
therapist. I'm her Gram.


00:05:18.104 --> 00:05:19.395
[Harper] All right,
well, this has been real.


00:05:19.478 --> 00:05:21.345
Please drive away like
you don't know me.


00:05:22.046 --> 00:05:23.114
Make good choices!


00:05:23.249 --> 00:05:25.242
-You are so lame.
-[horn honking]


00:05:25.377 --> 00:05:26.449
Lame!


00:05:26.851 --> 00:05:29.005
[in British accent] Are you
ready for laboratory today?


00:05:29.088 --> 00:05:30.413
Shut your mouth. [chuckles]


00:05:30.549 --> 00:05:31.617
[bell ringing]


00:05:31.753 --> 00:05:33.682
[teacher] Fun bonus round today.


00:05:33.818 --> 00:05:36.129
Never trust an atom. Why?


00:05:38.024 --> 00:05:40.024
'Cause they make up
everything. [chuckles]


00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:41.793
Here all day, folks.


00:05:41.929 --> 00:05:43.346
You're supposed to
put your goggles on


00:05:43.429 --> 00:05:44.632
before we start.


00:05:45.402 --> 00:05:47.071
The goggles are giving Minion.


00:05:47.206 --> 00:05:49.038
Yeah. We're not, like, Minions.


00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:52.543
So, no, thank you. But
they're perfect for you.


00:05:53.313 --> 00:05:55.207
It's like the Revolutionary War


00:05:55.342 --> 00:05:56.342
was for nothing.


00:05:56.614 --> 00:06:00.351
Today, remember, these
are dangerous chemicals.


00:06:00.486 --> 00:06:02.131
Maybe we should use
not-dangerous chemicals?


00:06:02.214 --> 00:06:03.841
How about you do your
actual share of the work


00:06:03.924 --> 00:06:05.124
instead of doodling?


00:06:05.259 --> 00:06:06.659
[lab partner] It's
called designing.


00:06:06.953 --> 00:06:08.624
The measurements
have to be precise.


00:06:09.327 --> 00:06:10.889
This experiment is so simple.


00:06:11.024 --> 00:06:13.223
In the UK, we did this
in primary school.


00:06:14.093 --> 00:06:15.827
The only reason people
think you're smart


00:06:15.962 --> 00:06:18.070
is because of your
obnoxious accent.


00:06:18.206 --> 00:06:20.664
At least people
think I'm clever.


00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.105
What's that supposed to mean?


00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.210
You're smart. Figure it out.


00:06:26.407 --> 00:06:27.471
-Oh, no.
-Oh, no.


00:06:27.606 --> 00:06:28.672
-Oh, no.
-Oh, no.


00:06:28.808 --> 00:06:30.183
[Harper, lab partner] Oh, no.


00:06:30.783 --> 00:06:31.783
Oh!


00:06:32.519 --> 00:06:35.782
-That was not precise!
-That's not precise at all!


00:06:36.891 --> 00:06:38.948
Oh. Principal Waldman!


00:06:39.083 --> 00:06:40.409
I don't know, Mom.
I don't know why


00:06:40.492 --> 00:06:41.972
the principal called
me, but I'm here.


00:06:42.088 --> 00:06:43.512
So you don't need to
come. You know what?


00:06:43.595 --> 00:06:44.940
I can't find what I was
gonna tell you about.


00:06:45.023 --> 00:06:46.823
-I'll call you...
-[grunts]


00:06:46.958 --> 00:06:48.367
-Sorry.
-It's totally my fault.


00:06:48.502 --> 00:06:50.799
No, no, no. I-I wasn't
looking where I was going.


00:06:50.935 --> 00:06:52.062
Oh.


00:06:58.771 --> 00:07:00.404
-Are you okay?
-[sighs]


00:07:00.539 --> 00:07:01.740
[phone ringing]


00:07:01.876 --> 00:07:03.382
-[stammers] Your phone.
-Yeah, I...


00:07:03.517 --> 00:07:05.879
Yeah, I don't know how
to turn this thing off.


00:07:06.014 --> 00:07:07.779
Yeah, I'm not sure,
either. I think, maybe...


00:07:07.915 --> 00:07:09.155
-I think you got it.
-Is it off?


00:07:09.257 --> 00:07:10.715
-Yeah. It's just...
-Oh, thank you.


00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:12.315
-No problem.
-Thank you.


00:07:12.451 --> 00:07:13.451
[sighs]


00:07:13.557 --> 00:07:15.895
Um, my daughter
just started here,


00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.430
and I admit I'm quite lost.


00:07:17.565 --> 00:07:19.416
Would you happen to know
where the chemistry lab is?


00:07:19.499 --> 00:07:22.158
This is serious. Someone
could have been injured.


00:07:22.293 --> 00:07:24.013
I'm sure it was just
an accident. [chuckles]


00:07:24.601 --> 00:07:26.739
It seems to me a
misunderstanding.


00:07:26.874 --> 00:07:29.572
Harper seems so...


00:07:30.502 --> 00:07:31.574
lovely.


00:07:31.709 --> 00:07:35.681
Oh. Well, Lily seems
so genuine and kind.


00:07:35.816 --> 00:07:37.348
[both chuckling]


00:07:37.484 --> 00:07:40.449
Wow. I certainly
never had two parents


00:07:40.585 --> 00:07:42.414
come in here and
be this attractive.


00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:44.149
I meant "attentive."


00:07:44.285 --> 00:07:45.457
Oh.


00:07:45.592 --> 00:07:47.925
Uh, Lily and I are
definitely going to reflect


00:07:48.061 --> 00:07:49.956
on how to do better.


00:07:50.092 --> 00:07:53.559
This is all Harper and I
are going to think about.


00:07:53.694 --> 00:07:56.225
We're very, very committed.


00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:00.563
Especially as a
single-parent household.


00:08:00.698 --> 00:08:01.832
Oh, us too.


00:08:01.967 --> 00:08:03.368
-We're single. Parent.
-Great.


00:08:03.504 --> 00:08:04.504
I mean, uh...


00:08:04.875 --> 00:08:07.303
-I'm a single parent, yeah.
-Single parent. Great.


00:08:07.438 --> 00:08:09.381
-Yeah. You know what I mean.
-Yes. Same. Me too.


00:08:09.948 --> 00:08:10.949
Single.


00:08:11.084 --> 00:08:12.541
Single parent. Guilty.


00:08:12.676 --> 00:08:13.609
Great.


00:08:13.744 --> 00:08:14.945
I'm single too.


00:08:15.081 --> 00:08:16.555
Oh, my God... Should we meet up?


00:08:16.690 --> 00:08:18.952
Perhaps our daughters should
get to know each other?


00:08:19.088 --> 00:08:21.620
Maybe, like, Wednesdays,
after 6:00. Get a little wine?


00:08:21.756 --> 00:08:23.490
Talk about these badass kids?


00:08:23.626 --> 00:08:25.225
Harper would really like that.


00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:26.492
Over dinner?


00:08:26.627 --> 00:08:27.866
Dinner sounds perfect.


00:08:28.002 --> 00:08:29.227
[Waldman] I'm on it.


00:08:30.331 --> 00:08:33.796
<i>Petit Trois</i>? Yes, can
I have a table for two?


00:08:33.931 --> 00:08:36.174
Private. In the back.


00:08:36.309 --> 00:08:37.810
Do you guys have any allergies?


00:08:37.945 --> 00:08:39.009
-No.
-No.


00:08:39.144 --> 00:08:40.210
No. No allergies.


00:08:40.346 --> 00:08:42.975
[♪ "Heart Attack" playing]


00:09:29.563 --> 00:09:32.460
[Tess] Okay, you came
here early. Spill it.


00:09:32.595 --> 00:09:33.860
[Anna] There's just no time.


00:09:33.995 --> 00:09:35.761
Bachelorette party,
dance rehearsal,


00:09:35.896 --> 00:09:37.628
final fitting, rehearsal lunch.


00:09:37.764 --> 00:09:39.231
And, oh, my wedding.


00:09:39.366 --> 00:09:42.340
You have a lot on your
plate. Big day. Deep breath.


00:09:42.476 --> 00:09:44.067
There's so much to
do before Sunday.


00:09:44.203 --> 00:09:45.644
Anna, let us know
how we can help.


00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.288
Maybe someone could help me
memorize my wedding vows.


00:09:47.371 --> 00:09:48.858
[Harper] How about
this? I'll help you.


00:09:48.941 --> 00:09:50.647
"I, Anna, take you, Eric,


00:09:50.782 --> 00:09:53.647
a man that I have been
dating for six months,


00:09:53.782 --> 00:09:55.613
but might uproot my entire life


00:09:55.749 --> 00:09:57.182
and move to London,


00:09:57.317 --> 00:10:00.359
"where we have no family
and an avocado costs $11."


00:10:00.495 --> 00:10:02.318
Perhaps you should
add something about


00:10:02.453 --> 00:10:05.459
my undying patience
for teenage rebellion.


00:10:05.595 --> 00:10:06.612
Spot on about the avocado.


00:10:06.695 --> 00:10:08.161
Oh. That wasn't about you.


00:10:08.296 --> 00:10:10.760
It was actually about my
mom's other British fiancé.


00:10:10.896 --> 00:10:12.062
She's a comedian today.


00:10:12.198 --> 00:10:13.486
-Just today, though.
-I see. Yeah.


00:10:13.569 --> 00:10:14.735
[Anna] Right, Harper?


00:10:14.871 --> 00:10:16.087
I have been practicing
our first dance.


00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.650
Wait till you see
what I have cooking.


00:10:17.773 --> 00:10:19.804
Ooh, I see what you did there.


00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:21.739
I missed you since yesterday.


00:10:21.875 --> 00:10:23.474
-Ew.
-[chuckles]


00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:26.178
[radio host] <i>Trevor Travis
just dropped a new single.</i>


00:10:26.314 --> 00:10:28.316
<i>I think we can all guess
who it might be about.</i>


00:10:28.452 --> 00:10:29.612
[music playing on radio]


00:10:29.747 --> 00:10:30.985
Hello?


00:10:31.421 --> 00:10:32.757
[horn blares]


00:10:32.893 --> 00:10:35.851
I had my pastry chef make
sticky toffee pudding pavlova


00:10:35.986 --> 00:10:37.188
for the bake sale.


00:10:37.323 --> 00:10:39.697
Just what every
teenager loves. Pavlova.


00:10:39.832 --> 00:10:42.425
Agreed. Teenagers these
days, sophisticated palates.


00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:46.538
Yes, well, this pastry
chef was up at 4:00 a.m.


00:10:46.673 --> 00:10:48.668
baking old-fashioned
chocolate chip cookies


00:10:48.803 --> 00:10:50.503
from scratch, with no staff.


00:10:50.639 --> 00:10:53.004
Four hours for cookies?


00:10:53.139 --> 00:10:55.041
I think we need to
get you a staff.


00:10:56.712 --> 00:10:58.174
They just needed to cool.


00:10:58.310 --> 00:10:59.815
Stand up straight. Good posture.


00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:01.435
Okay. And do you know
how bad this is for you?


00:11:01.518 --> 00:11:03.318
Seriously, eat this.


00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:05.353
Say, "Thanks, Mom."


00:11:05.489 --> 00:11:06.419
I saw that, Harper.


00:11:06.555 --> 00:11:07.486
[horn honking]


00:11:07.621 --> 00:11:09.055
Any day now.


00:11:10.158 --> 00:11:11.823
Just trying to keep
us on a schedule here.


00:11:11.959 --> 00:11:13.190
[in British accent] Oi. Well,


00:11:13.326 --> 00:11:15.527
we wouldn't want to be
off schedule, innit?


00:11:15.662 --> 00:11:16.662
Step, and...


00:11:16.761 --> 00:11:17.827
Hi, Lil!


00:11:17.962 --> 00:11:18.962
[Lily] It's Lily.


00:11:19.072 --> 00:11:20.598
Lily, back seat.


00:11:21.234 --> 00:11:22.627
[normal voice] Can't
Grams just take me?


00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.635
No, this will be good
bonding for everyone.


00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:27.038
Well, I bond best with Lily


00:11:27.174 --> 00:11:28.390
when we're not
around each other,


00:11:28.473 --> 00:11:30.305
and I don't have to
look at her face.


00:11:30.441 --> 00:11:32.217
Yeah, I love
sitting next to you.


00:11:32.352 --> 00:11:33.811
Reminds me that I'm amazing.


00:11:33.947 --> 00:11:35.246
[Tess] Seat belts, girls.


00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:42.557
-[horn honks]
-[both laughing]


00:11:42.692 --> 00:11:43.988
[Ryan] All right. All right.


00:11:44.123 --> 00:11:45.287
-I got you.
-You got me.


00:11:45.422 --> 00:11:47.061
-Good morning.
-We're ready to go.


00:11:47.197 --> 00:11:49.697
Good morning. Car's all
set. Up the coast, Route 1?


00:11:49.833 --> 00:11:52.266
-Yeah?
-Yeah? What do you think?


00:11:52.401 --> 00:11:55.374
[Tess] I'm not saying I don't
not want to go on the trip.


00:11:55.510 --> 00:11:58.774
I'm just saying
that Anna's wedding


00:11:58.909 --> 00:12:00.642
has put me behind
with my patients,


00:12:00.777 --> 00:12:02.710
which has been very disruptive.


00:12:02.846 --> 00:12:05.348
-Uh-huh.
-And... And, of course,


00:12:05.817 --> 00:12:08.454
they keep adding
dates to my book tour,


00:12:08.589 --> 00:12:10.849
which, you know, it's
out of my control.


00:12:11.318 --> 00:12:12.918
And I'm just saying
I need a little time.


00:12:13.051 --> 00:12:14.385
Look, girls. [sighs]


00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.861
We're trying to hear you.
Just try and hear us?


00:12:16.997 --> 00:12:18.089
Oh, no.


00:12:18.224 --> 00:12:19.594
I hear you trying
to pull me away


00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.130
from my family and my friends.


00:12:22.266 --> 00:12:24.832
I mean, who even gets to
surf before school in London?


00:12:24.968 --> 00:12:27.267
You can surf on
the river Thames.


00:12:27.403 --> 00:12:28.700
Really?


00:12:28.835 --> 00:12:29.966
No, you dipstick.


00:12:30.102 --> 00:12:31.300
-Girls.
-It's a city.


00:12:31.436 --> 00:12:32.756
-You need to...
-Okay, girls. Girls.


00:12:32.839 --> 00:12:33.940
It's our decision.


00:12:34.342 --> 00:12:36.546
Eric and I will do what's
right for the family.


00:12:36.681 --> 00:12:37.907
-Hmm.
-[Harper] Family?


00:12:38.042 --> 00:12:39.176
Yes, this family.


00:12:39.312 --> 00:12:40.816
-Don't say it like that.
-Don't say...


00:12:40.952 --> 00:12:42.133
-That sounds really cringe.
-Don't tell me


00:12:42.216 --> 00:12:43.598
-what to say and how to say.
-[sighs]


00:12:43.681 --> 00:12:44.965
[Lily] Harper, relax.
Don't be so dramatic.


00:12:45.048 --> 00:12:46.083
[Eric] Lily.


00:12:46.218 --> 00:12:47.922
-Stop gaslighting.
-What?


00:12:48.057 --> 00:12:50.256
You don't even know
what that means.


00:12:50.391 --> 00:12:51.713
[Harper] I don't wanna
look at your face anymore.


00:12:51.796 --> 00:12:53.393
You know what that means, right?


00:12:53.529 --> 00:12:54.849
-I think I know what it means.
-[Anna] Yeah. I knew you did.


00:12:54.932 --> 00:12:56.561
That explains why
you talk rubbish.


00:12:56.697 --> 00:12:59.762
[Waldman] <i>For the bake sale,
every table must have...</i>


00:12:59.897 --> 00:13:01.333
Okay.


00:13:01.469 --> 00:13:02.622
<i>...a gluten-free option,
an egg-free option...</i>


00:13:02.705 --> 00:13:04.368
Please don't slam the...


00:13:05.804 --> 00:13:06.902
door.


00:13:07.572 --> 00:13:09.405
Well, at least we don't
have to bring them


00:13:09.541 --> 00:13:11.512
to our immigration
interview tomorrow.


00:13:12.115 --> 00:13:14.613
Don't be stressed.
They'll come round.


00:13:15.382 --> 00:13:17.887
Yeah, let them take
all the time they need.


00:13:19.324 --> 00:13:21.790
[artist singing]


00:13:21.926 --> 00:13:23.523
He sounds great. I'll
be back in a bit.


00:13:24.159 --> 00:13:25.956
-Here's Ella's schedule.
-Thank you.


00:13:26.558 --> 00:13:28.180
Oh, send those to the
tour manager, please.


00:13:28.263 --> 00:13:30.326
-Yeah, okay.
-[singer] Okay? Because I'm...


00:13:30.462 --> 00:13:32.264
-I'm a pop star on the rise.
-Okay.


00:13:32.399 --> 00:13:33.954
[singer] So I wanna do
the album, you know.


00:13:34.037 --> 00:13:35.184
We can come in here
after midnight.


00:13:35.267 --> 00:13:36.805
I got the keys to the studio.


00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.634
-How's it going?
-Oh, good morning.


00:13:38.770 --> 00:13:40.871
Actually, it's literally
not. It's a bad morning.


00:13:41.007 --> 00:13:42.140
It's a very bad morning.


00:13:42.276 --> 00:13:43.879
Not for me, personally,
but for you.


00:13:44.015 --> 00:13:45.579
-Why, what happened?
-[inhales deeply]


00:13:45.715 --> 00:13:47.014
Trevor dumped Ella.


00:13:47.149 --> 00:13:48.847
And he already released
a song about it.


00:13:48.982 --> 00:13:51.457
<i>-Anna!
-Oh.</i>


00:13:51.592 --> 00:13:53.250
Yeah, and he dumped
her in a text.


00:13:53.385 --> 00:13:55.151
-Yeah, I got this.
-Toxic icon.


00:13:55.821 --> 00:13:58.458
I'll get in the booth, and
I'ma just lay it all down...


00:13:59.161 --> 00:14:00.542
[Anna] Okay, so
Trevor wrote a song.


00:14:00.625 --> 00:14:02.525
But I'm sure it's not
as bad as you think.


00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.399
It's called "Better
Than the Last One."


00:14:04.535 --> 00:14:05.870
It's about me.


00:14:06.005 --> 00:14:08.571
Okay, but that title, it
could be about anyone.


00:14:08.707 --> 00:14:10.870
It says, parentheses, "Ella."


00:14:11.006 --> 00:14:12.270
Let's just focus on the songs


00:14:12.406 --> 00:14:14.343
that you're gonna
perform on Saturday.


00:14:14.478 --> 00:14:15.738
Performing! Yay!


00:14:15.873 --> 00:14:20.046
I can't sing those songs.
I wrote them about Trevor.


00:14:20.181 --> 00:14:22.251
I put my heart and
soul into them.


00:14:22.386 --> 00:14:25.850
No, a 44-year-old Dutch music
producer wrote those songs.


00:14:26.586 --> 00:14:28.656
[Trevor] ♪ <i>She's
nothing like my ex</i> ♪


00:14:28.792 --> 00:14:30.320
This is a hit! This is...


00:14:30.456 --> 00:14:32.022
I can't even stop
moving my body.


00:14:32.158 --> 00:14:33.357
-Shh!
-Look, my chest


00:14:33.492 --> 00:14:34.852
-is just gyrating. I can't...
-Off!


00:14:35.526 --> 00:14:37.197
Oh, turn it off.
Turn... All right.


00:14:39.335 --> 00:14:41.498
What is that? Did you
learn that from Oprah?


00:14:41.633 --> 00:14:43.193
[student 1] Join the
Environmental Club.


00:14:43.306 --> 00:14:45.094
[student 2] Come over.
We have the best cookies.


00:14:45.177 --> 00:14:46.654
[Simon] Welcome to the
great Sunset Ridge Bake-Off.


00:14:46.737 --> 00:14:48.942
Shouldn't these be more
prominently featured?


00:14:49.077 --> 00:14:50.474
<i>Bon Appétit</i> literally profiled


00:14:50.609 --> 00:14:52.129
my dad's restaurant
for these pastries.


00:14:52.215 --> 00:14:55.077
I think they're nice
and prominent over here.


00:14:55.213 --> 00:14:56.452
Uh, they're gourmet.


00:14:56.588 --> 00:14:58.121
They're soggy-bottomed.


00:14:58.257 --> 00:15:01.419
You know what? I think I see
the perfect spot for yours.


00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.595
-Just...
-Dude!


00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.591
-Those were Gram's!
-Come on.


00:15:05.727 --> 00:15:10.895
You know what? I think I know
the perfect place to put this.


00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:13.136
You wouldn't dare.


00:15:13.272 --> 00:15:14.531
[sighs]


00:15:15.606 --> 00:15:17.468
-[gasps]
-Oh.


00:15:18.972 --> 00:15:20.542
Yeah. Perfect.


00:15:20.678 --> 00:15:21.938
Nice caramelization.


00:15:22.073 --> 00:15:24.479
Oh. Just...


00:15:24.614 --> 00:15:25.744
[students gasp]


00:15:25.879 --> 00:15:27.011
Oh, my God.


00:15:27.146 --> 00:15:28.882
[♪ "Oh!" playing]


00:15:29.017 --> 00:15:32.351
[mouthing words] Food fight!


00:15:33.491 --> 00:15:35.019
Food fight!


00:15:35.155 --> 00:15:37.829
-Oh, no!
-[screaming]


00:15:40.331 --> 00:15:42.733
[Harper's friend] They're
attacking us from above!


00:15:42.869 --> 00:15:44.935
[student 3] We need
the high ground!


00:15:46.471 --> 00:15:49.401
[clamoring]


00:15:51.039 --> 00:15:52.470
[student 3] On my signal!


00:15:53.975 --> 00:15:56.540
[distorted yelling]


00:16:00.718 --> 00:16:02.254
[Lily] Too far, Harper.


00:16:02.723 --> 00:16:04.615
Stop it! Put that down! Stop it.


00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.819
Give me that. Give me that.
Put that down. Stop it!


00:16:06.955 --> 00:16:08.425
No, not the strudel!


00:16:08.561 --> 00:16:10.796
Please! Or the tart.


00:16:19.939 --> 00:16:22.401
Stop it! That got
in my mouth! Hey!


00:16:24.703 --> 00:16:26.576
[Waldman] You want a
fight? Let's fight!


00:16:26.711 --> 00:16:30.145
[distorted clamoring]


00:16:30.979 --> 00:16:32.884
[distorted gasping]


00:16:37.555 --> 00:16:39.187
[gasping]


00:16:42.593 --> 00:16:44.625
[exhales deeply]


00:16:44.761 --> 00:16:46.392
Who started...


00:16:47.433 --> 00:16:48.559
the food fight?


00:16:50.868 --> 00:16:52.334
Congratulations, you two.


00:16:52.469 --> 00:16:55.104
You just got everybody in
here in-school suspension.


00:16:55.239 --> 00:16:57.035
-[students groaning]
-[student] Thanks a lot.


00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.107
Is this key lime pie?


00:16:59.242 --> 00:17:01.407
Yeah, I baked it
fresh this morning.


00:17:01.542 --> 00:17:03.197
Well, you gotta take me
to the emergency room


00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:06.017
because I'm very
allergic to key lime pie.


00:17:06.453 --> 00:17:10.450
[Anna, through headphones] ♪
<i>I just keep on coming back</i> ♪


00:17:10.585 --> 00:17:13.556
♪ <i>I'm your good
And I'm your...</i> ♪


00:17:13.692 --> 00:17:15.292
[Ella] Is this you?


00:17:15.428 --> 00:17:16.742
[through speakers] ♪ <i>Baby,
our love was made...</i> ♪


00:17:16.825 --> 00:17:18.323
Oh, uh...


00:17:18.459 --> 00:17:20.332
That's not supposed
to be in there.


00:17:20.801 --> 00:17:22.031
-Was it for Pink Slip?
-Hmm.


00:17:22.167 --> 00:17:24.298
I saw them at the
Troubadour last year.


00:17:26.203 --> 00:17:28.370
Could I sing your
song this weekend?


00:17:28.506 --> 00:17:29.766
Oh, no.


00:17:29.901 --> 00:17:31.456
You'll have way better stuff
than something I wrote.


00:17:31.539 --> 00:17:33.543
I wrote that after I
left Pink Slip anyway.


00:17:33.678 --> 00:17:36.447
Okay. I got this.


00:17:36.582 --> 00:17:37.782
Yes, you got this.


00:17:37.917 --> 00:17:39.782
Opening your world
tour at the Wiltern


00:17:39.917 --> 00:17:42.921
is a big show for you. Huge.


00:17:43.986 --> 00:17:45.553
For the both of us.


00:17:45.688 --> 00:17:47.508
The girls are struggling with
this transition, and just...


00:17:47.591 --> 00:17:50.261
just take it from a parent
who has been in your shoes.


00:17:50.396 --> 00:17:53.362
I know, Tess, between losing
Lily's mum and moving here...


00:17:53.498 --> 00:17:56.597
Yes, and being ripped away
from the home she grew up in.


00:17:56.732 --> 00:17:58.718
Oh, I'm sorry. Are we talking
about Lily or about Harper?


00:17:58.801 --> 00:17:59.836
Harp? Lily?


00:17:59.971 --> 00:18:01.189
[Tess] That is really annoying.


00:18:01.272 --> 00:18:02.788
-[Eric] No, it's just...
-Hey. What the...


00:18:02.871 --> 00:18:04.302
What's going on?


00:18:04.437 --> 00:18:05.674
-Darling...
-No one's hurt.


00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:06.877
I went to the school...


00:18:07.013 --> 00:18:08.253
Please let me just handle this.


00:18:09.346 --> 00:18:11.311
Anna, there's been
an incident at school


00:18:11.446 --> 00:18:12.951
between the girls.
It was really bad.


00:18:13.086 --> 00:18:17.218
-What bad? How bad? Oh...
-[Eric] I've got this.


00:18:17.354 --> 00:18:19.624
Girls, apologize to
each other now, please.


00:18:19.759 --> 00:18:21.958
Ooh, honey, forced apologies


00:18:22.094 --> 00:18:23.141
is never a way to
resolve conflict.


00:18:23.224 --> 00:18:24.690
-That...
-[Eric] But...


00:18:24.826 --> 00:18:27.394
We need to make space for
them to express how they feel.


00:18:27.863 --> 00:18:28.961
[exhales deeply]


00:18:29.097 --> 00:18:31.233
Harper, how do you feel?


00:18:32.604 --> 00:18:34.305
I feel...


00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:35.440
sorry.


00:18:36.039 --> 00:18:37.910
And, Lily, how do you feel?


00:18:38.545 --> 00:18:39.839
I feel... [sighs]


00:18:39.975 --> 00:18:40.774
...sorry too.


00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:41.910
That's great.


00:18:42.043 --> 00:18:43.444
-Great.
-See?


00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.268
Sorry that my future
stepsister is a complete twit.


00:18:45.351 --> 00:18:46.837
I'm sorry that my future
stepsister is a shallow idiot.


00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:48.777
-Oh, am I? Really?
-New plan!


00:18:48.912 --> 00:18:50.284
No more holding
space for feelings.


00:18:50.419 --> 00:18:52.019
You two are gonna
have a lovely time


00:18:52.154 --> 00:18:53.518
at my bachelorette tonight.


00:18:53.654 --> 00:18:54.976
You're gonna get along
because we're a family,


00:18:55.059 --> 00:18:56.357
and families love each other!


00:18:56.492 --> 00:18:58.127
And for that, Harper,
just for that look,


00:18:58.263 --> 00:19:01.566
you two earned yourself
a sleepover at Gram's.


00:19:01.701 --> 00:19:03.197
Huh? Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:19:03.333 --> 00:19:06.266
Why am I the punishment?
I'm the fun one.


00:19:06.402 --> 00:19:07.901
-I have board games.
-[Harper] Mom.


00:19:08.036 --> 00:19:09.304
I have Parcheesi.


00:19:09.439 --> 00:19:10.960
And you're gonna braid
each other's hair


00:19:11.043 --> 00:19:12.740
in a non
cultural-appropriating way


00:19:12.875 --> 00:19:13.676
and like it.


00:19:13.811 --> 00:19:15.212
What is Parcheesi?


00:19:15.347 --> 00:19:16.925
-[Tess] It's a game.
-[Eric] I'm not quite sure.


00:19:17.008 --> 00:19:18.331
You move around the
board. You shake the dice.


00:19:18.414 --> 00:19:19.979
You remember the
sound of the dice?


00:19:20.114 --> 00:19:20.914
Oh, it's amazing.


00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.117
You get these dice,


00:19:22.253 --> 00:19:23.516
and you shake 'em in your hand,


00:19:23.651 --> 00:19:25.214
-you move around the board.
-Oh, Grams.


00:19:25.349 --> 00:19:26.349
It's really fun.


00:19:26.484 --> 00:19:27.916
I also have Boggle!


00:19:28.052 --> 00:19:30.556
You stay on your side,
and I'll stay on mine.


00:19:31.596 --> 00:19:32.822
Gladly.


00:19:33.831 --> 00:19:35.000
Harper, look,


00:19:35.135 --> 00:19:36.481
I know you think I
don't get it, but I do.


00:19:36.564 --> 00:19:38.169
And it's still just
gonna be you and me.


00:19:38.304 --> 00:19:41.433
If you go to London, I'm
staying here with Grams.


00:19:41.569 --> 00:19:43.341
-She said it was cool.
-She what?


00:19:43.476 --> 00:19:47.310
Hey, Anna! Did you remove me
as Harper's secondary contact?


00:19:47.445 --> 00:19:50.078
Did you tell Harper that
she could stay here with you


00:19:50.213 --> 00:19:52.175
if we decided to move to London?


00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:53.310
[stammers]


00:19:53.715 --> 00:19:56.085
-Are you serious right now?
-Whoa. Are you serious?


00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:57.399
-[Tess] Okay, okay.
-Why are you...


00:19:57.482 --> 00:19:58.851
[Tess] What is serious


00:19:58.986 --> 00:20:02.254
is that you and Eric need to
keep the girls in Los Angeles.


00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.893
Lily just needs some guidance.


00:20:05.295 --> 00:20:06.855
The only guidance
I need from you


00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:08.429
is to show me to
the other bathroom.


00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:12.097
I'm very sorry, Lily.
I didn't know...


00:20:12.233 --> 00:20:13.299
You don't know anything


00:20:13.435 --> 00:20:15.438
about what I need or how I feel,


00:20:15.573 --> 00:20:18.203
or the fashion school back
home that I wanna go to.


00:20:18.339 --> 00:20:19.642
-[door slams]
-Oh!


00:20:20.011 --> 00:20:22.377
Yep. Just you and me, Mom.


00:20:22.911 --> 00:20:23.813
Great.


00:20:23.948 --> 00:20:25.415
[DJ] <i>Welcome, everyone,</i>


00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.877
<i>to the bachelorette
party of our girl, Anna.</i>


00:20:31.683 --> 00:20:33.921
[Harper groans] Mom, for real?


00:20:34.057 --> 00:20:35.786
[Harper] Why would you?


00:20:35.921 --> 00:20:38.086
-[Anna] Haven't changed.
-[Maddie] Not a bit.


00:20:38.789 --> 00:20:41.358
-[guest] Anna!
-It's so funny.


00:20:41.493 --> 00:20:42.194
[guest] Get it, girl!


00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:43.696
I remember that six-pack.


00:20:43.832 --> 00:20:45.821
-[Harper] Yeah, who is that?
-[Maddie] So handsome.


00:20:45.904 --> 00:20:47.769
[Peg] That is Jake.


00:20:48.238 --> 00:20:49.732
[Maddie] Your mom's first love.


00:20:49.868 --> 00:20:51.866
[Peg] And her first
ride on a motorcycle.


00:20:52.002 --> 00:20:54.812
I like to ride in
Jake's motorcycle.


00:20:54.947 --> 00:20:56.147
-Okay.
-[guests chuckle]


00:20:56.282 --> 00:20:58.308
[Maddie] Jake also
had a thing for Tess.


00:20:58.444 --> 00:20:59.679
[Harper] For Grams?


00:20:59.814 --> 00:21:01.563
All right, okay. Enough
humiliation for the night.


00:21:01.646 --> 00:21:03.484
[♪ Rock music playing]


00:21:16.059 --> 00:21:19.336
Harper, baby, I
made you a plate.


00:21:19.472 --> 00:21:22.030
Here you go. You're too
young to be sad. Come on.


00:21:22.165 --> 00:21:24.334
Well, being young is
overrated, Mama P.


00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:25.506
Eat. You'll be fine.


00:21:26.376 --> 00:21:28.839
[Mama P exclaims] Use the tongs.


00:21:34.554 --> 00:21:35.912
[sighs]


00:21:42.892 --> 00:21:44.129
[sighs]


00:21:48.594 --> 00:21:51.268
Lily? Mind if I join you?


00:21:55.306 --> 00:21:57.807
You know, Anna lost her father


00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:01.069
around the same age that
you lost your mother.


00:22:02.746 --> 00:22:06.077
And then she had to deal
with my wedding to Ryan.


00:22:06.212 --> 00:22:07.542
Cool.


00:22:08.344 --> 00:22:12.421
And then you add to that
the complications of moving.


00:22:13.485 --> 00:22:14.522
I'm here for you.


00:22:16.454 --> 00:22:17.822
Sincerely.


00:22:20.992 --> 00:22:23.359
With all due
respect, Dr. Coleman,


00:22:23.895 --> 00:22:26.095
you're not my gran
or my therapist.


00:22:26.231 --> 00:22:28.437
So, while I get your motive
for keeping us in LA,


00:22:29.172 --> 00:22:30.406
I don't need your help.


00:22:34.737 --> 00:22:35.938
[exhales sharply]


00:22:36.073 --> 00:22:38.347
[Anna] Oh, no. We
used to be so cool.


00:22:38.483 --> 00:22:41.176
-Hey, I'm still cool.
-I look amazing.


00:22:41.312 --> 00:22:43.169
You're very cool. That
song you sent me was sick.


00:22:43.252 --> 00:22:44.385
-Yeah.
-Thank you.


00:22:44.521 --> 00:22:46.148
I wish I had more time to write.


00:22:46.284 --> 00:22:48.218
But now all I do is listen
to parenting podcasts.


00:22:48.353 --> 00:22:51.620
Well, I'm sorry for ruining
your exciting rock star life.


00:22:51.756 --> 00:22:53.187
Harper, wait. I was just...


00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:55.266
Wait, I wasn't serious.


00:22:55.401 --> 00:22:57.435
Look, I gave up
performing, but I have you.


00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:01.036
-[Harper] Enjoy your party.
-[Anna] You can't leave.


00:23:01.439 --> 00:23:03.239
I don't think I
belong in here, Grams.


00:23:03.375 --> 00:23:04.586
Let me handle
this. I've got you.


00:23:04.669 --> 00:23:06.101
-[Anna] Harper!
-Anna,


00:23:06.236 --> 00:23:08.703
honey, you just need
to pause and reframe.


00:23:08.839 --> 00:23:10.246
-Thanks, Mom.
-What?


00:23:10.382 --> 00:23:11.876
-What did I do?
-I was handling it.


00:23:12.011 --> 00:23:13.662
And you completely
undermine me as a parent.


00:23:13.745 --> 00:23:14.843
I was trying to help you.


00:23:14.978 --> 00:23:16.063
Well, your help isn't helpful.


00:23:16.146 --> 00:23:17.980
Well, that's not
very nice to say.


00:23:18.116 --> 00:23:20.852
Can the great and
mysterious Madame Jen


00:23:20.987 --> 00:23:23.494
interest you ladies
in a psychic reading?


00:23:24.330 --> 00:23:26.690
[chuckles] No.
Thank you very much,


00:23:26.826 --> 00:23:28.632
but, um, right now is not the...


00:23:28.767 --> 00:23:29.958
Time?


00:23:30.094 --> 00:23:31.829
-It's just not really our...
-Thing?


00:23:31.965 --> 00:23:34.538
This will all be over
soon, if you just...


00:23:35.408 --> 00:23:37.173
-Go with it.
-Go with it. Yes, exactly.


00:23:37.308 --> 00:23:38.508
-Come on in. Yes. Yes.
-No. No.


00:23:38.641 --> 00:23:40.136
-Come.
-Okay, I'm coming. Here we go.


00:23:40.271 --> 00:23:41.495
-Anybody else interested?
-Let's try this out.


00:23:41.578 --> 00:23:43.098
I do discounts for
bigger groups. Okay?


00:23:43.183 --> 00:23:44.847
Okay. That's fine. That's good.


00:23:44.982 --> 00:23:46.247
[door locks]


00:23:46.383 --> 00:23:47.843
And that's how I lost my spot


00:23:47.978 --> 00:23:49.417
at the Larchmont
Farmers' Market.


00:23:49.553 --> 00:23:51.982
But I did get a
table by the lids


00:23:52.117 --> 00:23:54.556
and free milk counter
inside of the Starbucks.


00:23:54.691 --> 00:23:58.626
So, I am a life coach,
but I also do Reiki.


00:23:58.762 --> 00:24:00.897
If you notice, I have
several business cards,


00:24:01.033 --> 00:24:02.100
because I actually have


00:24:02.236 --> 00:24:04.562
a business-card-making business.


00:24:04.698 --> 00:24:05.781
So, that's the card for that.


00:24:05.864 --> 00:24:07.269
Uh, I can put quotes on there


00:24:07.405 --> 00:24:09.264
that I can just make up for you.


00:24:09.400 --> 00:24:11.736
If you want something
inspirational, for example,


00:24:11.872 --> 00:24:14.143
I can make up a
quote like, um...


00:24:14.279 --> 00:24:16.538
"Live your life... [stammers]


00:24:16.674 --> 00:24:17.775
Gosh dang it."


00:24:17.911 --> 00:24:19.231
-Okay.
-[Madame Jen] So, here's...


00:24:19.353 --> 00:24:24.055
And-And-And I'm gonna
read your palms now.


00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:25.554
-'Cause that's...
-[Tess] Really?


00:24:27.058 --> 00:24:28.058
[Madame Jen sighs]


00:24:28.194 --> 00:24:32.695
Okay. And there they go. Yes.


00:24:33.398 --> 00:24:35.190
[mumbles] Eenie,
meeney, miney...


00:24:35.759 --> 00:24:37.225
[sniffs] Hmm.


00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:40.498
Okay. It smells like
you had some appetizers.


00:24:40.634 --> 00:24:41.666
-Were they good?
-Good.


00:24:41.801 --> 00:24:43.233
-Good. Yes.
-Yeah. Yes.


00:24:43.769 --> 00:24:45.376
And did you have any, Mom?


00:24:46.811 --> 00:24:50.171
-Um, no. Mm-mmm. No. I didn't.
-I'm... No. No. Didn't...


00:24:50.307 --> 00:24:51.947
-'Cause I paid for them.
-I paid for them.


00:24:52.080 --> 00:24:55.177
-It's a wedding. Okay.
-[babbles] Okay. Okay, okay.


00:24:55.312 --> 00:24:59.291
Your life lines. It...
It's like they've...


00:25:01.819 --> 00:25:03.628
intersected before.


00:25:04.131 --> 00:25:05.589
-How strange.
-Really?


00:25:05.724 --> 00:25:06.957
[Madame Jen stammers]


00:25:07.092 --> 00:25:10.458
You've walked in
each other's path.


00:25:11.428 --> 00:25:16.973
It's like a crazy
path-cross that you've done.


00:25:17.108 --> 00:25:19.377
[gasps, straining]


00:25:22.041 --> 00:25:23.742
[distorted] You've
learned a lesson.


00:25:23.878 --> 00:25:26.175
A lesson that may
serve you again.


00:25:26.310 --> 00:25:27.978
-Okay. That's enough.
-Thank you. Okay.


00:25:28.113 --> 00:25:29.634
[Tess] We'll give
these to my neighbors.


00:25:29.717 --> 00:25:31.053
[normal] I'm onto
something here.


00:25:31.189 --> 00:25:33.987
One more thing. [sighs]


00:25:34.123 --> 00:25:36.722
Right over there is a QR code
that you can tip me with.


00:25:36.857 --> 00:25:38.923
Any amount is
appreciated. Really.


00:25:39.058 --> 00:25:40.696
I didn't know I
could do that voice.


00:25:40.831 --> 00:25:43.460
-Nice prank. Ha-ha.
-Yeah, we know what you did.


00:25:43.596 --> 00:25:44.629
What did I do?


00:25:44.765 --> 00:25:46.263
What do you mean? The psychic.


00:25:46.399 --> 00:25:48.282
-Yeah. Telling her about...
-[Mama P] What... Okay, okay.


00:25:48.365 --> 00:25:50.903
You think I'd rather
solve your problem


00:25:51.038 --> 00:25:54.269
than deal with my
booming culinary empire.


00:25:54.404 --> 00:25:57.614
♪ <i>I just thought Think about</i> ♪


00:25:57.749 --> 00:25:59.408
♪ <i>All the things you
can And can't get</i> ♪


00:25:59.544 --> 00:26:01.743
-I'm following you because...
-You're happy here, so...


00:26:01.879 --> 00:26:03.045
Are you the psychic?


00:26:03.181 --> 00:26:04.408
I need you to look
into my future


00:26:04.491 --> 00:26:05.770
and tell me where
we're going to live.


00:26:05.853 --> 00:26:08.592
Oh. Cool Gen Z talking to me.


00:26:08.728 --> 00:26:10.956
If it's not London, I need
you to alter my destiny.


00:26:11.091 --> 00:26:13.259
And I literally have
to stay in Los Angeles,


00:26:13.394 --> 00:26:14.430
so, if there's...


00:26:14.566 --> 00:26:16.368
Well, that's not
really how it works.


00:26:17.169 --> 00:26:18.799
Well, how does it work?


00:26:19.868 --> 00:26:24.303
Girls, follow my
aura. [chuckles]


00:26:24.438 --> 00:26:26.801
Boop. Beep.


00:26:26.937 --> 00:26:28.504
[mimics pushing buttons]


00:26:28.639 --> 00:26:29.859
[Madame Jen] You don't have
a lot of lines in your hands,


00:26:29.942 --> 00:26:31.093
so it makes it harder for me.


00:26:31.176 --> 00:26:33.143
You two are called to be family.


00:26:33.278 --> 00:26:35.948
-Yeah, right.
-[scoffs] Don't remind me.


00:26:37.783 --> 00:26:39.314
A lesson for you all.


00:26:41.786 --> 00:26:43.318
I see it now.


00:26:43.863 --> 00:26:45.056
[gasps]


00:26:48.094 --> 00:26:50.060
Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:26:50.195 --> 00:26:52.997
to reach the place
where you belong.


00:26:53.132 --> 00:26:55.098
Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:26:55.233 --> 00:26:57.635
to reach the place
where you belong.


00:26:58.204 --> 00:27:00.301
Change the hearts
you know are wrong...


00:27:00.437 --> 00:27:02.639
Why is she rhyming
like a bridge troll?


00:27:03.241 --> 00:27:05.944
Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:27:06.079 --> 00:27:08.847
to reach the place
where you belong.


00:27:08.983 --> 00:27:11.350
-Change the hearts...
-Earthquake.


00:27:11.485 --> 00:27:13.018
Earthquake?


00:27:13.153 --> 00:27:15.889
-[rumbling]
-[music in venue slows down]


00:27:18.888 --> 00:27:20.124
[rumbling stops]


00:27:22.025 --> 00:27:23.929
[distorted yelling]


00:27:24.064 --> 00:27:26.127
[singer, normal]
♪ <i>Here and now</i> ♪


00:27:26.262 --> 00:27:28.000
[slow] ♪<i> Here and now</i> ♪


00:27:36.808 --> 00:27:38.010
Did you feel that?


00:27:39.375 --> 00:27:42.080
Yeah, I... It must
be the dancing.


00:27:42.615 --> 00:27:44.017
Yeah, right.


00:27:44.152 --> 00:27:46.032
We're just freaking
ourselves out for no reason.


00:27:46.119 --> 00:27:48.483
-Yeah. It's just in our heads.
-Right.


00:27:48.618 --> 00:27:50.555
[radio announcer] <i>With
your surf forecast...</i>


00:27:50.691 --> 00:27:52.224
All cozy and tucked in?


00:27:52.360 --> 00:27:54.328
<i>Fearless prediction for
the full moon tonight...</i>


00:27:54.463 --> 00:27:55.733
[exhales sharply]


00:27:56.135 --> 00:27:57.364
You need anything?


00:27:57.834 --> 00:27:59.361
What more could I possibly need?


00:27:59.496 --> 00:28:01.533
[Harper] How about
sleeping in our own beds


00:28:01.668 --> 00:28:02.699
in our own rooms?


00:28:02.835 --> 00:28:04.476
-Hmm.
-Hmm.


00:28:06.046 --> 00:28:07.270
Sweet dreams.


00:28:08.543 --> 00:28:09.841
[Tess scoffs]


00:28:09.976 --> 00:28:11.082
-Teenagers.
-[Anna sighs]


00:28:11.217 --> 00:28:12.513
[Anna] I was one once.


00:28:12.649 --> 00:28:14.385
[Tess] Yeah, so was I. Twice.


00:28:14.521 --> 00:28:16.154
-[Tess] Night.
-[Anna] Night. Love you.


00:28:16.289 --> 00:28:17.417
[Tess] Love you too, honey.


00:28:17.552 --> 00:28:19.216
[thunder rumbles]


00:28:37.768 --> 00:28:40.105
[Madame Jen] <i>Change the
hearts you know are wrong</i>


00:28:40.241 --> 00:28:42.976
<i>to reach the place
where you belong.</i>


00:28:43.112 --> 00:28:45.209
<i>Change the hearts
you know are wrong</i>


00:28:45.345 --> 00:28:47.446
<i>to reach the place
where you belong.</i>


00:28:47.581 --> 00:28:50.016
[alarm ringing]


00:28:53.219 --> 00:28:55.791
[Harper groans] <i>I
don't have an alarm.</i>


00:28:57.994 --> 00:28:59.797
[Harper] <i>Why do my
hands look so dry?</i>


00:28:59.933 --> 00:29:01.126
[grunts]


00:29:01.896 --> 00:29:03.260
[Harper] <i>Why am I so tired?</i>


00:29:05.567 --> 00:29:06.828
[Harper] <i>Mom?</i>


00:29:06.963 --> 00:29:08.236
[Anna] Mom?


00:29:09.005 --> 00:29:10.498
-[Harper] <i>Grams?</i>
-[Anna] Grams?


00:29:14.138 --> 00:29:18.311
Grams. Grams, are you okay?


00:29:19.014 --> 00:29:21.945
Why are you bloody
waking me up for?


00:29:22.080 --> 00:29:24.120
-Are you mad?
-Mad?


00:29:24.489 --> 00:29:25.650
Why do I sound like this?


00:29:25.786 --> 00:29:27.284
[Anna] Sound like what?


00:29:27.918 --> 00:29:29.319
American!


00:29:31.187 --> 00:29:33.261
[gasping, grunting]


00:29:33.397 --> 00:29:35.798
Oh. Good. Mom.


00:29:36.532 --> 00:29:37.595
What was that?


00:29:37.730 --> 00:29:40.329
Ow! Oh. Ow!


00:29:40.465 --> 00:29:42.970
-[sighs]
-[Harper] Lily, are you okay?


00:29:43.605 --> 00:29:45.434
I'm not Lily.


00:29:51.073 --> 00:29:52.342
Are you Harper?


00:29:53.712 --> 00:29:55.042
No.


00:29:55.178 --> 00:29:59.285
No. No. No, no, no.


00:29:59.921 --> 00:30:03.452
-I'm bloody decomposing!
-Oh, my.


00:30:03.921 --> 00:30:06.554
[both screaming]


00:30:07.793 --> 00:30:09.130
[both gasp]


00:30:09.266 --> 00:30:10.159
Harper?


00:30:10.294 --> 00:30:12.460
-Oh, my God.
-[Harper] Whoa.


00:30:12.596 --> 00:30:14.015
-What is happening?
-[Harper] I know.


00:30:14.098 --> 00:30:15.733
It's me, Harp. It's Mom.


00:30:15.869 --> 00:30:17.303
What are you saying?


00:30:17.439 --> 00:30:20.106
So if you're me and I'm you,
then... then who is that?


00:30:20.841 --> 00:30:22.273
I'm Grandma, sweetheart.


00:30:24.645 --> 00:30:26.277
[screams]


00:30:28.145 --> 00:30:30.648
Oh, my gosh! I've died.


00:30:30.783 --> 00:30:33.020
I killed myself!


00:30:33.155 --> 00:30:35.820
She just has crevices
all over her face.


00:30:35.955 --> 00:30:37.592
Look at the crevices.


00:30:37.728 --> 00:30:39.527
My hands look like doll hands.


00:30:39.662 --> 00:30:41.497
My butt feels so high.


00:30:41.633 --> 00:30:42.891
I think I just peed a little.


00:30:43.026 --> 00:30:44.161
[Harper] Oh, no.


00:30:44.296 --> 00:30:47.699
My face feels so
thirsty and dry.


00:30:47.835 --> 00:30:50.166
My face is perfect.


00:30:50.301 --> 00:30:52.434
My face looks like a Birkin bag


00:30:52.570 --> 00:30:56.274
that's been left out
in the sun to rot.


00:30:56.808 --> 00:30:57.808
Why?


00:30:57.912 --> 00:30:59.508
Why do I have to pee again?


00:30:59.643 --> 00:31:02.077
This is so much weirder
than the last time.


00:31:02.213 --> 00:31:03.915
Last time? What last time?


00:31:04.050 --> 00:31:05.616
How come you never told me?


00:31:05.751 --> 00:31:07.875
[Harper] We never told anyone,
sweetheart. Overnight oats.


00:31:07.958 --> 00:31:09.485
Now let's just
pause and reframe.


00:31:09.620 --> 00:31:11.553
No. I didn't want to be
a part of this family


00:31:11.689 --> 00:31:14.828
and now I'm part of
some dodgy family curse?


00:31:14.963 --> 00:31:16.832
-And I'm the eldest?
-Mom.


00:31:16.967 --> 00:31:20.336
And where are her
lips? She has no lips!


00:31:20.471 --> 00:31:21.471
Where did they go?


00:31:21.573 --> 00:31:22.798
[Anna] How do we fix this?


00:31:23.601 --> 00:31:25.281
Well, you know, last
time, we switched back


00:31:25.406 --> 00:31:27.709
when we saw things from
the other's perspective.


00:31:27.844 --> 00:31:28.974
[Lily] Should we hold hands?


00:31:29.109 --> 00:31:30.291
-Hold my hands.
-Well, we can...


00:31:30.374 --> 00:31:32.149
-Just... [clears throat]
-Yeah.


00:31:32.819 --> 00:31:34.577
I know I've been
hard on you and Eric,


00:31:34.712 --> 00:31:37.351
but I can now see that
you're doing the right thing.


00:31:37.487 --> 00:31:43.189
And, Mom, you have always done
so much for me, and I see you.


00:31:47.827 --> 00:31:49.296
I see you.


00:31:49.431 --> 00:31:50.817
-Are you really seeing me?
-Mm-hmm. I really see you.


00:31:50.900 --> 00:31:52.233
Because I don't feel anything.


00:31:52.368 --> 00:31:54.771
You have no idea how hard
I'm seeing you right now.


00:31:54.907 --> 00:31:56.568
-[Tess] One, two, three.
-[Anna] ...three.


00:31:57.271 --> 00:31:58.937
[groans] Girls,
that doesn't work.


00:31:59.073 --> 00:32:00.536
Yeah, we tried that last time.


00:32:01.743 --> 00:32:03.174
Looking like this


00:32:03.310 --> 00:32:06.079
is why people like
you become shut-ins,


00:32:06.215 --> 00:32:08.785
and what's with this
accent? "Tomato."


00:32:08.920 --> 00:32:10.787
Is that what you
think I sound like?


00:32:10.922 --> 00:32:12.138
[in British accent]
Oh, my God, yes.


00:32:12.221 --> 00:32:14.122
Of course this is
what you sound like.


00:32:14.257 --> 00:32:15.603
-Let's go to Erewhon...
-I do not sound like that.


00:32:15.686 --> 00:32:17.958
I've never said that.
I don't even know...


00:32:18.094 --> 00:32:19.892
Then I need to call
my energy healer


00:32:20.028 --> 00:32:21.359
because I need a chakra reset.


00:32:21.494 --> 00:32:23.801
-That's what you sound like.
-The healer.


00:32:24.732 --> 00:32:25.862
Madame Jen.


00:32:26.231 --> 00:32:27.563
I thought she was a psychic.


00:32:27.699 --> 00:32:29.806
Ow. I thought she did
sound baths for dogs.


00:32:29.941 --> 00:32:31.574
I thought she was
a water sommelier.


00:32:31.710 --> 00:32:32.941
She did try to sell me knives.


00:32:33.077 --> 00:32:35.471
[stammers] What? No,
well, whatever she is,


00:32:35.607 --> 00:32:38.447
we have to find her,
but until then...


00:32:38.582 --> 00:32:39.749
"Until then" what?


00:32:39.885 --> 00:32:41.676
Last time we convinced everyone


00:32:41.811 --> 00:32:43.568
that we were each other
until we switched back.


00:32:43.651 --> 00:32:47.253
Oh, brilliant. So how are we
supposed to pull that off?


00:32:47.389 --> 00:32:50.157
Well, panicking is not
going to help anyone!


00:32:50.292 --> 00:32:51.852
-I need you to get dressed.
-This sucks!


00:32:51.961 --> 00:32:53.928
-Go. Go get...
-No! Stop.


00:32:54.064 --> 00:32:55.892
Bye, girls. It's
going to be great.


00:32:56.027 --> 00:32:57.429
Look, Mom.


00:32:57.564 --> 00:32:59.219
I kept it totally together
in front of the girls,


00:32:59.302 --> 00:33:02.202
but I have to be honest, I
am freaking out right now!


00:33:02.337 --> 00:33:04.602
That was you keeping
it totally together?


00:33:04.738 --> 00:33:05.574
Yes!


00:33:05.709 --> 00:33:07.273
No, no. Just checking.


00:33:08.108 --> 00:33:09.307
[Lily] Aura photographer.


00:33:09.443 --> 00:33:11.315
Hmm. Twenty percent
off on her Etsy shop.


00:33:11.451 --> 00:33:12.451
I can't get married.


00:33:12.544 --> 00:33:13.949
I haven't even had
a boyfriend yet.


00:33:14.084 --> 00:33:15.817
We have to switch
back to our bodies.


00:33:16.352 --> 00:33:20.291
At least your body didn't
wake up with arthritis.


00:33:20.426 --> 00:33:21.816
It's disconnected.


00:33:21.951 --> 00:33:23.572
I guess her life coaching
business went bust.


00:33:23.655 --> 00:33:25.528
I'm supposed to get
married this weekend.


00:33:25.663 --> 00:33:27.030
[Tess] What are these?


00:33:27.165 --> 00:33:29.461
And how many puffer
jackets does someone need?


00:33:29.596 --> 00:33:32.168
-Hmm. Reiki master. [gasps]
-What? What'd you find?


00:33:32.737 --> 00:33:36.733
I bent down and didn't toot.


00:33:37.569 --> 00:33:39.272
Youth really is
wasted on the young.


00:33:39.407 --> 00:33:43.806
And what's with the old
tissues in every pocket?


00:33:43.942 --> 00:33:45.216
Explain.


00:33:45.351 --> 00:33:46.110
[dial tone]


00:33:46.246 --> 00:33:48.214
No answer at Reiki. Now what?


00:33:48.350 --> 00:33:49.977
Did you try her vegan
meat loaf truck?


00:33:50.113 --> 00:33:52.136
They don't have a number,
and they only use DoorDash,


00:33:52.219 --> 00:33:53.368
and I don't know how to do that.


00:33:53.451 --> 00:33:57.191
I look Eileen Fisher years old.


00:33:58.058 --> 00:34:00.360
I'm literally my mother.


00:34:00.495 --> 00:34:02.863
I'm going to need therapy
for the rest of my life


00:34:02.998 --> 00:34:04.264
and not the kind from Grams.


00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:07.504
Like the real kind that
you have to pay for.


00:34:07.973 --> 00:34:09.806
[groans] Why does
anyone wear these?


00:34:09.942 --> 00:34:11.907
Did she say anything,
like a fortune?


00:34:12.043 --> 00:34:14.943
No, but maybe she
told the girls.


00:34:15.079 --> 00:34:16.710
[Harper] Did the
psychic say anything


00:34:16.846 --> 00:34:18.311
to you about a fortune?


00:34:18.446 --> 00:34:20.347
It could be the key to
getting out of this.


00:34:21.217 --> 00:34:22.484
-Wait, she did, right?
-She did.


00:34:22.619 --> 00:34:23.821
What was it?


00:34:23.956 --> 00:34:26.021
"Change the hearts
you know are wrong


00:34:26.156 --> 00:34:28.486
to reach the place
where you belong."


00:34:28.621 --> 00:34:31.218
[gasps] That's about our
parents getting married.


00:34:31.353 --> 00:34:33.830
LA. London.


00:34:33.966 --> 00:34:36.859
As teenagers, we have no power.


00:34:36.994 --> 00:34:41.939
No say in whether we move
or stay, but as adults...


00:34:43.305 --> 00:34:45.199
Mom, she didn't
say anything to us!


00:34:45.334 --> 00:34:46.170
[screams]


00:34:46.306 --> 00:34:48.874
-[Harper grunting]
-Oh.


00:34:49.009 --> 00:34:50.608
Whoa. Anna. Anna!


00:34:50.743 --> 00:34:52.529
You do not hit me. I am
your mother, young lady.


00:34:52.612 --> 00:34:55.117
-So, what do you say?
-[Harper] Well, then...


00:34:55.253 --> 00:34:57.652
-[Harper] It's not working!
-We need a plan.


00:34:57.788 --> 00:34:58.951
[Lily] Not my fault!


00:34:59.520 --> 00:35:01.388
-DK doughnuts!
-[Harper] She'll love those.


00:35:01.523 --> 00:35:03.403
-Harper, got 'em.
-[Harper] I... I'll love them.


00:35:03.523 --> 00:35:05.661
Hey, girls. How
was the sleepover?


00:35:05.796 --> 00:35:07.325
-Good.
-Very good.


00:35:07.461 --> 00:35:08.999
-We did teenager stuff.
-Very good.


00:35:11.000 --> 00:35:12.132
[Tess] So here's our plan.


00:35:12.268 --> 00:35:14.635
First, these
clothes are rubbish.


00:35:14.771 --> 00:35:15.938
I just can't.


00:35:16.074 --> 00:35:20.472
Can you just give
me five minutes?


00:35:33.185 --> 00:35:34.490
-What?
-Oh, no.


00:35:34.625 --> 00:35:36.057
How? Why?


00:35:36.193 --> 00:35:37.507
[Tess] <i>You're in
your mum's body,</i>


00:35:37.590 --> 00:35:39.729
so all you have to
do is tell my dad


00:35:39.864 --> 00:35:41.631
you don't love him anymore.


00:35:41.766 --> 00:35:42.896
Wedding is off. Done.


00:35:43.031 --> 00:35:45.794
Whoa. Got some bangs.


00:35:45.929 --> 00:35:47.999
-What did you do to my hair?
-I fixed it.


00:35:48.135 --> 00:35:49.268
And you're welcome.


00:35:49.404 --> 00:35:50.805
-It's called a fringe.
-Fixed it.


00:35:50.941 --> 00:35:52.239
You don't seriously think


00:35:52.375 --> 00:35:53.953
you're going to my
work dressed like this.


00:35:54.036 --> 00:35:55.461
Take that off. You're
going to get me fired.


00:35:55.544 --> 00:35:56.633
-What'd you do to my hair?
-I straightened it.


00:35:56.716 --> 00:35:57.949
You never wash your hair.


00:35:58.084 --> 00:35:59.499
No, I don't. The ocean
washes it for me.


00:35:59.582 --> 00:36:01.776
[Tess] <i>Obviously, the
wedding can't happen.</i>


00:36:01.912 --> 00:36:03.368
It's Friday. We only
have till Sunday.


00:36:03.451 --> 00:36:05.255
We gotta do some
serious sabotage.


00:36:05.391 --> 00:36:07.915
<i>The immigration interview,
the rehearsal lunch.</i>


00:36:08.051 --> 00:36:11.825
Then what if we cancel
all the wedding stuff?


00:36:11.961 --> 00:36:13.894
The cake, place, people.


00:36:14.030 --> 00:36:15.495
Yes, and all we have to do


00:36:15.630 --> 00:36:18.200
is convince our parents
that they are incompatible.


00:36:18.335 --> 00:36:20.630
Which should not be hard
because my mom obviously


00:36:20.766 --> 00:36:23.137
should not be with some
wannabe Gordon Ramsay.


00:36:23.272 --> 00:36:25.537
Well, my father
doesn't want to be


00:36:25.673 --> 00:36:29.977
with some wannabe Valley
Village rocker mom.


00:36:30.113 --> 00:36:32.716
I quite like this, sexy tiger.


00:36:32.852 --> 00:36:33.981
-Doughnut!
-It's, um...


00:36:34.117 --> 00:36:35.447
It's an American superstition


00:36:35.583 --> 00:36:37.005
that it's bad luck for
the bride and groom


00:36:37.088 --> 00:36:38.820
to kiss before
they say I do so...


00:36:38.955 --> 00:36:40.748
Really? For how long?


00:36:40.883 --> 00:36:42.957
For a long time.
A long, long time.


00:36:43.093 --> 00:36:44.561
-Really?
-Yeah. Also, uh...


00:36:44.696 --> 00:36:45.927
no touching hands.


00:36:46.063 --> 00:36:47.326
No touching at all. [chuckles]


00:36:47.462 --> 00:36:49.161
No gazing into each other's eyes


00:36:49.297 --> 00:36:51.527
because it's gross. Um, yeah.


00:36:51.663 --> 00:36:53.093
-How odd.
-For maximum luck.


00:36:53.229 --> 00:36:56.430
[Tess] And finally, we
must be convincing as them


00:36:56.566 --> 00:36:57.899
until we break them up.


00:37:00.403 --> 00:37:01.336
[Ryan] Lily?


00:37:01.472 --> 00:37:02.541
-What?
-Yeah?


00:37:03.939 --> 00:37:05.713
Did you just take
Tess's calcium?


00:37:05.848 --> 00:37:07.084
[Lily] Mmm.


00:37:11.656 --> 00:37:12.881
[Tess] Mmm.


00:37:13.757 --> 00:37:14.982
Bone health.


00:37:16.991 --> 00:37:18.226
You need those.


00:37:18.362 --> 00:37:19.844
-You need those.
-Yes, I'll be taking them.


00:37:19.927 --> 00:37:21.331
Okay.


00:37:21.466 --> 00:37:23.076
-You need to take those.
-Give me the doughnut back.


00:37:23.159 --> 00:37:24.619
-No. You're very diabetic.
-[Eric] Okay, girls.


00:37:24.702 --> 00:37:26.193
Let's crack on.


00:37:26.796 --> 00:37:28.261
-[all] Oh.
-[Harper] Um...


00:37:28.397 --> 00:37:31.004
Well, actually, uh, Lily and
I aren't feeling very well.


00:37:31.140 --> 00:37:32.267
We think it might be a...


00:37:32.402 --> 00:37:33.339
My throat.


00:37:33.475 --> 00:37:34.903
...smart decision to stay home.


00:37:35.038 --> 00:37:37.580
This has nothing to do
with your detention?


00:37:37.715 --> 00:37:39.249
Oh. Uh...


00:37:39.384 --> 00:37:42.453
Well, you wouldn't want
me to go to school sick,


00:37:42.588 --> 00:37:43.588
would you, Mom?


00:37:43.687 --> 00:37:45.012
Hmm.


00:37:45.891 --> 00:37:46.953
You don't feel sick to me.


00:37:47.689 --> 00:37:49.951
Does she look sick to
you, Grams? I mean, Mom?


00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:53.687
No. They look fine.


00:37:53.822 --> 00:37:55.022
You have your client Ella's


00:37:55.157 --> 00:37:56.857
huge<i> Rolling Stone</i>
photo shoot today


00:37:56.992 --> 00:37:58.466
and your immigration interview.


00:37:58.601 --> 00:38:01.035
Don't you need a little
bit of help with that, hmm?


00:38:01.171 --> 00:38:02.768
Of course she needs your help.


00:38:02.904 --> 00:38:03.904
[scoffs]


00:38:04.007 --> 00:38:05.307
Right? Kids these days.


00:38:05.442 --> 00:38:07.235
They'll say anything
to get out of school.


00:38:07.371 --> 00:38:09.495
-All right. Come on. Let's go.
-Go on. And make good choices.


00:38:09.578 --> 00:38:11.944
-See you at the dance studio!
-Bye! What?


00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:13.341
Dance studio?


00:38:14.177 --> 00:38:16.276
Let's go. Change at the
club. I've got your bag.


00:38:16.412 --> 00:38:17.346
Change?


00:38:17.482 --> 00:38:18.347
This is the finals.


00:38:18.483 --> 00:38:19.484
Welcome, everybody,


00:38:19.620 --> 00:38:22.055
to the Westside
Pickleball Championship.


00:38:22.458 --> 00:38:25.052
Yeah. You have your
championship today.


00:38:26.031 --> 00:38:27.228
I think you're gonna be late.


00:38:27.363 --> 00:38:29.693
Late? Yes! Yeah,
I'm gonna be late.


00:38:29.829 --> 00:38:31.187
[dance instructor]
<i>Okay, newlyweds,</i>


00:38:31.270 --> 00:38:33.871
<i>you just made your
grand entrance</i>


00:38:34.006 --> 00:38:35.537
<i>into the wedding reception.</i>


00:38:35.673 --> 00:38:40.144
The lights begin to dim. And
a five, six, seven, Eric.


00:38:41.280 --> 00:38:44.346
-[instructor] Beth, no.
-Oh, right. Like a bull.


00:38:45.344 --> 00:38:46.380
[instructor] Yes!


00:38:46.516 --> 00:38:49.118
-Charging. It's a bull. Yes.
-Stallion.


00:38:49.254 --> 00:38:51.453
Get it, groom. Big
stallion energy.


00:38:51.588 --> 00:38:53.307
-[Beth] It's a bull, though.
-[instructor] All right.


00:38:53.390 --> 00:38:54.790
-[instructor] So look at him.
-What?


00:38:54.919 --> 00:38:55.942
[instructor] Eye
contact, come on.


00:38:56.025 --> 00:38:57.453
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:38:57.588 --> 00:38:59.627
Tango is your pelvis.


00:38:59.762 --> 00:39:01.995
[commentator 1] Pickleball.
It's a sport like tennis


00:39:02.131 --> 00:39:03.430
but it is pathetic.


00:39:03.566 --> 00:39:05.299
Tennis for lazy people,
that's what it is.


00:39:05.435 --> 00:39:07.002
It's like tennis but
for non athletes.


00:39:07.137 --> 00:39:08.502
It's a bunch of old nutters


00:39:08.637 --> 00:39:10.403
with giant paddles
chasing a Wiffle ball.


00:39:10.539 --> 00:39:12.539
It's not bloody
Wimbledon, is it?


00:39:13.437 --> 00:39:14.437
Here we go.


00:39:15.071 --> 00:39:17.881
-That's yours!
-Okay. That was so fast.


00:39:18.016 --> 00:39:19.313
[shrieks] Oh, so aggressive!


00:39:19.449 --> 00:39:21.475
-What was that?
-She almost hit me!


00:39:21.977 --> 00:39:23.812
-[Eric] Oh.
-[Anna] Okay.


00:39:24.348 --> 00:39:26.068
-[Eric] No. You're going down.
-[instructor] Up. Up you go.


00:39:26.151 --> 00:39:27.810
-I think you should go up.
-No, it's okay. It's fine.


00:39:27.893 --> 00:39:28.949
This is good right here.


00:39:29.085 --> 00:39:30.592
You're just lying on the floor.


00:39:31.161 --> 00:39:32.689
Taking a little nappy-poo.


00:39:32.825 --> 00:39:34.564
It's not a nappy-poo,
it's tango.


00:39:34.699 --> 00:39:37.125
Oh, no. I'm just thinking that
maybe tango isn't our dance.


00:39:37.260 --> 00:39:40.761
-Um, anything else?
-Beth, what else is sexy?


00:39:41.230 --> 00:39:42.863
Come on. Let's keep
our head in the game.


00:39:42.998 --> 00:39:45.341
-Whoo!
-Game point, suckers.


00:39:47.704 --> 00:39:49.477
[distorted breathing]


00:39:57.649 --> 00:39:59.780
-[screams]
-Drop in!


00:39:59.915 --> 00:40:01.685
-[shrieks]
-[grunts]


00:40:01.821 --> 00:40:03.192
Serena Williams,
she's got nothing


00:40:03.328 --> 00:40:04.774
on the sounds these
ladies are making.


00:40:04.857 --> 00:40:07.394
The body-thumping
beat of hip-hop.


00:40:07.530 --> 00:40:09.656
-Like that? Yep.
-Bop, bop, bop. Yes.


00:40:09.792 --> 00:40:10.992
A hop and a hip-hop.


00:40:11.128 --> 00:40:13.329
I've never seen this
kind of hip-hop.


00:40:13.464 --> 00:40:15.529
[Tess shrieking]


00:40:16.331 --> 00:40:17.719
-She's on the ground.
-How is she doing that?


00:40:17.802 --> 00:40:19.067
[opponent] That's a new move.


00:40:19.203 --> 00:40:21.476
That's defensive offense.
Defensive offense!


00:40:22.111 --> 00:40:23.247
Woman, get up!


00:40:25.777 --> 00:40:27.074
[opponent, distorted] Oh, no!


00:40:27.209 --> 00:40:28.917
-That was close!
-Wow! Did you see that?


00:40:29.052 --> 00:40:30.353
Did you see that?


00:40:32.257 --> 00:40:33.417
-Did we win?
-[crowd cheering]


00:40:33.517 --> 00:40:35.391
Yes! Yes!


00:40:37.696 --> 00:40:38.888
We won!


00:40:39.023 --> 00:40:40.139
[opponent] I believe
that was illegal


00:40:40.222 --> 00:40:41.248
and I'd like to
roll back the tapes


00:40:41.331 --> 00:40:42.491
and watch that one more time.


00:40:42.594 --> 00:40:43.928
Take that, boomers!


00:40:44.063 --> 00:40:45.450
-Okay. You know what, no.
-Okay, first of all...


00:40:45.533 --> 00:40:46.895
-Hold me back.
-You stay back.


00:40:47.031 --> 00:40:48.571
-We are not boomers.
-We're Gen X!


00:40:48.707 --> 00:40:51.768
-We are elder millennials.
-Some of the last millennials.


00:40:51.904 --> 00:40:53.468
-The finale.
-[Eric] The finale.


00:40:53.903 --> 00:40:56.473
And five, six, seven, eight.


00:40:56.609 --> 00:40:59.008
Go! And slide. That's it.


00:40:59.144 --> 00:41:01.784
[♪ "(I've Had) The Time
of My Life" playing]


00:41:01.920 --> 00:41:03.347
[Beth] Get it.


00:41:03.482 --> 00:41:04.688
To the side. Whoo!


00:41:04.823 --> 00:41:06.521
Get it. Yes!


00:41:07.390 --> 00:41:09.359
-Ow!
-[instructor grunts]


00:41:17.200 --> 00:41:19.067
[instructor] And Anna.


00:41:19.203 --> 00:41:20.395
-Run, girl.
-Run!


00:41:20.530 --> 00:41:21.732
Anna.


00:41:21.868 --> 00:41:23.172
-Come on, let's go.
-[Beth] Run!


00:41:23.307 --> 00:41:26.277
-Get it. Run. Run.
-Run.


00:41:27.746 --> 00:41:29.203
Anna.


00:41:30.549 --> 00:41:32.509
[Harper] Mom, we're supposed
to know where to go.


00:41:32.645 --> 00:41:33.977
[Lily] Act natural, honey.


00:41:34.113 --> 00:41:36.353
-Detention's that way.
-Can you tell... Okay.


00:41:44.991 --> 00:41:46.929
[Harper] I have an
immigration interview,


00:41:47.064 --> 00:41:48.699
a rehearsal lunch,


00:41:48.834 --> 00:41:52.793
Ella's big show, my wedding,
and I am stuck in detention!


00:41:52.929 --> 00:41:54.295
Well, I'm stuck here too.


00:41:54.430 --> 00:41:57.875
And it's the championships
for the entire Westside.


00:41:58.411 --> 00:42:01.710
Well, well, well.
Look who showed up.


00:42:02.280 --> 00:42:05.649
Lily Reyes and Harper Coleman.


00:42:06.185 --> 00:42:08.275
How have you not retired yet?


00:42:08.411 --> 00:42:11.716
The school had our
pension invested in crypto


00:42:12.085 --> 00:42:13.965
but since I'm not supposed
to complain about it,


00:42:14.086 --> 00:42:16.819
per my lawyer, it's
neither here nor there.


00:42:17.188 --> 00:42:19.788
So let's surrender
our devices Let's go.


00:42:20.357 --> 00:42:23.894
-Mr. Bates... Come on.
-We just got our phones back.


00:42:24.029 --> 00:42:26.430
-That's right. We love school.
-Here.


00:42:26.799 --> 00:42:28.036
[Mr. Bates] Thank you, Simon.


00:42:28.838 --> 00:42:32.670
And now it's time to prepare
for the most boring task


00:42:32.806 --> 00:42:34.902
you could ever possibly imagine.


00:42:35.038 --> 00:42:39.044
Sit there, read or think only.


00:42:39.413 --> 00:42:41.847
No screens, books.


00:42:42.414 --> 00:42:43.346
[groans]


00:42:43.481 --> 00:42:44.515
Wait.


00:42:45.051 --> 00:42:48.148
Does he mean hours of
uninterrupted peace?


00:42:48.283 --> 00:42:50.818
Wipe that look of
bliss off your face.


00:42:50.954 --> 00:42:52.790
Get over yourself, Elton.


00:42:52.926 --> 00:42:54.524
This is high school, not prison.


00:42:54.660 --> 00:42:56.131
Yeah, it's not a prison.


00:42:56.267 --> 00:42:57.994
Which, FYI, research shows


00:42:58.129 --> 00:42:59.936
is ineffective at
preventing recidivism.


00:43:00.071 --> 00:43:01.405
Yeah, "resisism".


00:43:01.540 --> 00:43:03.300
[Lily] You know, giving
back to the community


00:43:03.400 --> 00:43:06.300
is a lot more effective
than trapping people inside.


00:43:07.571 --> 00:43:08.808
Oh!


00:43:09.708 --> 00:43:11.448
You wanna go outside?


00:43:12.346 --> 00:43:13.617
Let us out.


00:43:13.752 --> 00:43:15.499
-[students] Yeah, let us out.
-[Harper] Let us out.


00:43:15.582 --> 00:43:17.683
Let us out. Let us out.


00:43:17.818 --> 00:43:21.686
-Let us out. Let us out.
-Outside.


00:43:22.088 --> 00:43:24.652
-Move it! Let's pick it up!
-[horn honking]


00:43:24.787 --> 00:43:25.954
Out of the way!


00:43:26.089 --> 00:43:28.096
We need to find Madame Jen, now.


00:43:28.232 --> 00:43:29.724
We need our phones.


00:43:30.260 --> 00:43:33.030
Come on, Reyes! You
run like my grandma.


00:43:33.865 --> 00:43:34.997
-Pick it up.
-Rude!


00:43:35.133 --> 00:43:37.441
Pick up the pace or
you'll pick up trash.


00:43:37.576 --> 00:43:39.102
[venue assistant]
<i>It's in two days.</i>


00:43:39.238 --> 00:43:40.796
Yeah, I know. I don't
care about the deposit.


00:43:40.879 --> 00:43:42.555
-<i> And the officiant?</i>
-That includes the officiant?


00:43:42.638 --> 00:43:44.092
-Cancel that, too. Thank you.
-[line disconnects]


00:43:44.175 --> 00:43:45.397
[Siri] <i>Call from
Jett. Answer it?</i>


00:43:45.480 --> 00:43:46.808
Is this for real? Yes.


00:43:46.944 --> 00:43:48.410
[Jett] <i>Where are you?</i>


00:43:48.545 --> 00:43:49.866
<i>The editor from</i>
Rolling Stone<i> is here.</i>


00:43:49.949 --> 00:43:51.455
<i>-Come on! Hurry up!</i>
-Oh, no.


00:43:51.590 --> 00:43:53.917
[editor] Remember,
it's the<i> Hungry Tour.</i>


00:43:54.053 --> 00:43:55.982
Trevor's allergic
to strawberries.


00:43:56.118 --> 00:43:57.527
[editor] Look sweet, Ella.


00:43:58.696 --> 00:44:00.828
-Ella's having a meltdown.
-Morning, Anna.


00:44:00.964 --> 00:44:04.167
Hello, my staff of people
that I see all the time.


00:44:04.303 --> 00:44:06.129
Can you sign off on the dress?


00:44:06.830 --> 00:44:07.764
Here's your juice.


00:44:07.899 --> 00:44:09.039
-Oh, thank you.
-Mm-hmm.


00:44:09.575 --> 00:44:11.904
All right, so she's
over here by this...


00:44:12.739 --> 00:44:14.038
-Girl, what?
-Ugh.


00:44:14.407 --> 00:44:16.942
-Why would you give me that?
-You yell at me if I don't.


00:44:17.077 --> 00:44:20.845
Anna. Jean shorts, rash
guard. Laundry day?


00:44:21.348 --> 00:44:24.912
[sighs] Let's talk about the
headline for the article.


00:44:25.047 --> 00:44:26.589
"It's giving It-Girl.


00:44:26.724 --> 00:44:29.686
Pop star queen Ella
slays down the house."


00:44:29.822 --> 00:44:31.522
-Wait, what?
-Or,


00:44:31.658 --> 00:44:33.122
"We're gagging, besties.


00:44:33.258 --> 00:44:35.625
Ella's new album
just hits different."


00:44:35.760 --> 00:44:37.194
No, no. Just stop.


00:44:37.330 --> 00:44:39.727
What deeply out-of-touch old
person came up with those?


00:44:40.130 --> 00:44:42.664
-You did.
-I did? Wow.


00:44:42.800 --> 00:44:44.100
Thanks, puss.


00:44:44.236 --> 00:44:45.754
Okay, I really need
you to focus on Ella...


00:44:45.837 --> 00:44:47.874
-Okay.
-[Ella sobbing]


00:44:51.545 --> 00:44:52.582
Do something.


00:44:54.612 --> 00:44:55.681
Ella?


00:44:56.317 --> 00:44:59.556
[Ella] Trevor unfollowed me.
And you know what that means?


00:45:00.420 --> 00:45:01.586
No.


00:45:01.721 --> 00:45:05.056
What it means is that


00:45:05.191 --> 00:45:08.492
the whole world knows
that he dumped me.


00:45:08.627 --> 00:45:10.531
It's everywhere!


00:45:11.100 --> 00:45:14.629
Okay. I am your manager,
so I'm gonna manage this.


00:45:14.764 --> 00:45:15.934
Okay.


00:45:16.070 --> 00:45:18.005
[Tess] Ryan, I really
do need to dash.


00:45:18.140 --> 00:45:20.273
But they said the photographer
is back in 5 minutes.


00:45:20.409 --> 00:45:21.636
Photographer?


00:45:21.771 --> 00:45:22.872
Yeah.


00:45:23.007 --> 00:45:24.306
For your new passport photo.


00:45:24.441 --> 00:45:25.859
The one you need for
the international part


00:45:25.942 --> 00:45:27.080
of your book tour?


00:45:27.216 --> 00:45:28.443
Oh, yes.


00:45:28.578 --> 00:45:32.414
I remember every detail
that you told me about me.


00:45:32.549 --> 00:45:36.153
Yeah. I got prescriptions,
you got the essentials.


00:45:37.557 --> 00:45:38.826
Essentials?


00:45:43.265 --> 00:45:44.568
Yes.


00:45:51.167 --> 00:45:53.203
Do I need all these things?


00:46:01.846 --> 00:46:04.016
I need that. Yes.


00:46:05.224 --> 00:46:07.283
Where does this go?


00:46:08.225 --> 00:46:09.417
[retches]


00:46:13.991 --> 00:46:17.297
What? Adult nappies?


00:46:17.432 --> 00:46:19.394
That is so lazy.


00:46:20.869 --> 00:46:23.035
-Oh, hey.
-Yes. Right here.


00:46:25.905 --> 00:46:27.136
-Fixodent?
-Yes.


00:46:27.272 --> 00:46:29.203
Isn't that toothpaste
for old people?


00:46:29.605 --> 00:46:32.374
No. This is for when
you lose your teeth.


00:46:36.750 --> 00:46:38.545
I'm gonna lose my teeth?


00:46:39.750 --> 00:46:40.686
No!


00:46:40.821 --> 00:46:42.253
[Mr. Bates] Okay, slowpokes.


00:46:42.388 --> 00:46:45.891
I want every blue spirulina
smoothie spill gone.


00:46:46.026 --> 00:46:47.992
I want every chia seed scraped.


00:46:48.128 --> 00:46:49.994
Every chewed piece
of organic gum


00:46:50.130 --> 00:46:51.926
on the bottoms of
these seats gone!


00:46:52.061 --> 00:46:53.061
Way to go, Harper.


00:46:53.164 --> 00:46:54.348
Use your nails if you have to.


00:46:54.431 --> 00:46:57.534
What? No, this was Lily's fault.


00:46:57.669 --> 00:46:58.906
Elton.


00:47:00.001 --> 00:47:01.471
Yeah?


00:47:01.606 --> 00:47:04.274
I understand that you feel
the need to prove a point


00:47:04.409 --> 00:47:07.246
because I publicly
undermined your authority.


00:47:07.382 --> 00:47:08.410
Oh!


00:47:09.849 --> 00:47:11.785
Do you understand me?


00:47:11.920 --> 00:47:13.132
This isn't restorative justice.


00:47:13.215 --> 00:47:14.515
I mean, if anything,


00:47:14.650 --> 00:47:17.024
you're making these kids
want to act out more.


00:47:17.160 --> 00:47:19.856
How does Lily always manage
to make things worse?


00:47:19.991 --> 00:47:21.358
It's a unique talent.


00:47:21.493 --> 00:47:23.249
I have connections on
the school board, Elton.


00:47:23.332 --> 00:47:26.627
Well, you're a stupid kid
and you have no connections,


00:47:26.762 --> 00:47:30.967
but you have earned,
along with everybody here,


00:47:31.103 --> 00:47:32.704
three more weeks of detention.


00:47:32.840 --> 00:47:35.005
-Oh, my...
-Lily!


00:47:35.141 --> 00:47:37.241
-Bro!
-Your royal highness.


00:47:38.076 --> 00:47:39.546
-Come on!
-My God!


00:47:39.681 --> 00:47:41.047
That was uncalled for.


00:47:41.182 --> 00:47:45.480
Let's all take a deep,
centering breath.


00:47:47.122 --> 00:47:48.369
[detention student]
Meditate on this!


00:47:48.452 --> 00:47:49.852
Take a deep breath
of this trash.


00:47:49.987 --> 00:47:51.222
[Tess] You ready?


00:47:51.891 --> 00:47:53.125
[photographer] Stunning.


00:47:53.923 --> 00:47:55.056
Wow.


00:47:55.191 --> 00:47:56.425
[muffled] Good, right?


00:47:58.002 --> 00:48:00.262
I think you're having
an allergic reaction.


00:48:00.397 --> 00:48:03.102
No, no, no, no.
It's lip plumper.


00:48:03.705 --> 00:48:04.705
I'm gonna get some ice.


00:48:04.840 --> 00:48:06.105
Okay, give me the ring light.


00:48:06.240 --> 00:48:08.239
And every bottle of
Benadryl I can find.


00:48:08.374 --> 00:48:10.510
[Tess, muffled] It's
lip plumper. No, Ryan.


00:48:10.646 --> 00:48:12.446
I don't have allergies.


00:48:12.582 --> 00:48:13.715
Oh. Okay, whatever.


00:48:13.851 --> 00:48:15.147
Do you have another ring light?


00:48:15.282 --> 00:48:16.629
-Like, a big ring light?
-[photographer] Sure.


00:48:16.712 --> 00:48:18.546
-And another thing. Can you...
-Yeah, okay.


00:48:18.681 --> 00:48:21.322
You hold the ring light.
I'll pose. Okay, ready?


00:48:21.457 --> 00:48:22.484
I got it.


00:48:26.629 --> 00:48:28.160
Let me look. Hold on.


00:48:29.161 --> 00:48:32.429
Oh, no. Just 10, maybe 15 more.


00:48:32.564 --> 00:48:35.871
I'll give you looks, okay?
All right, here I go.


00:48:38.405 --> 00:48:41.136
[Tess] "Dear Sir, must
cancel the wedding venue


00:48:41.272 --> 00:48:42.744
because the bride is horrible,


00:48:42.880 --> 00:48:44.972
as my daughter
always suspected."


00:48:45.107 --> 00:48:47.282
Oh! Who's Laura?


00:48:47.418 --> 00:48:48.944
Hello, hello.


00:48:49.079 --> 00:48:51.135
[Laura] <i>Hey, hon. I need your
approval on the author photo.</i>


00:48:51.218 --> 00:48:53.284
-Okay.
-<i> Texting it over now.</i>


00:48:54.052 --> 00:48:56.787
[Tess] Oh, no. No, no.


00:48:56.923 --> 00:48:58.394
That one's rubbish.


00:48:58.529 --> 00:49:00.223
I just took a new one.


00:49:00.359 --> 00:49:02.194
-I'm sending now.
-<i> Thanks.</i>


00:49:02.329 --> 00:49:06.528
Oh, look. Her phone has
the giant letter virus.


00:49:08.338 --> 00:49:09.632
Oh!


00:49:09.768 --> 00:49:12.841
Ryan. Is it possible for you
to drop me at Anna's work?


00:49:12.977 --> 00:49:14.290
[announcer] <i>Hey,
you Trevorheads.</i>


00:49:14.373 --> 00:49:15.733
<i>That was your boy,
Trevor Travis,</i>


00:49:15.844 --> 00:49:17.074
<i>with his brand-new song,</i>


00:49:17.209 --> 00:49:18.509
<i>"Better than the Last One."</i>


00:49:19.412 --> 00:49:21.208
My mom's biggest client
is having a meltdown.


00:49:21.344 --> 00:49:22.718
-Jett!
-I'm working!


00:49:22.854 --> 00:49:24.986
Trevor, her
boyfriend, dumped her.


00:49:26.358 --> 00:49:27.358
Trevor Travis?


00:49:27.685 --> 00:49:30.956
♪ <i>She's so much better Better</i> ♪


00:49:31.091 --> 00:49:32.459
♪ <i>Better than the</i> ♪


00:49:32.828 --> 00:49:35.295
♪ <i>Last one</i> ♪


00:49:35.431 --> 00:49:36.531
[gasps]


00:49:37.033 --> 00:49:39.867
And they just got
matching tattoos.


00:49:40.002 --> 00:49:44.205
That is literally
the worst thing


00:49:44.341 --> 00:49:47.709
I have ever heard happening
to anyone ever, full stop.


00:49:47.844 --> 00:49:49.671
-Thank you.
-Of course.


00:49:50.207 --> 00:49:51.714
Anna's getting married,


00:49:51.850 --> 00:49:52.778
so she doesn't
get what it's like


00:49:52.914 --> 00:49:54.211
to have your heart broken.


00:49:54.347 --> 00:49:56.752
I know. When I was
your age, my mom...


00:49:56.888 --> 00:49:59.449
I mean, I had this
boyfriend, Jake,


00:49:59.585 --> 00:50:02.019
and all my friends say
he was my first love.


00:50:02.155 --> 00:50:04.159
Is that who your song's about?


00:50:04.562 --> 00:50:06.126
What song? My song?


00:50:12.434 --> 00:50:15.003
[Anna, through speakers]
♪ <i>See you in my dreams</i> ♪


00:50:16.406 --> 00:50:19.968
♪ <i>Whenever you go I
tear at the seams</i> ♪


00:50:20.104 --> 00:50:21.038
I wrote that?


00:50:21.173 --> 00:50:24.045
[chuckles] It's really good.


00:50:24.912 --> 00:50:27.416
This is a great song.


00:50:27.552 --> 00:50:29.716
You're really good.


00:50:30.152 --> 00:50:32.119
I don't get why
you quit playing.


00:50:33.525 --> 00:50:35.047
Because I had a kid


00:50:35.183 --> 00:50:38.856
who I probably resent since
I'm writing songs in secret.


00:50:38.992 --> 00:50:40.831
So, you miss performing?


00:50:42.633 --> 00:50:44.964
I mean, yeah, probably.


00:50:45.399 --> 00:50:47.904
I'm finding out a lot
about myself today.


00:50:49.003 --> 00:50:50.498
-[music stops]
-[sighs]


00:50:50.634 --> 00:50:54.140
Anna, your song is
the only song I loved


00:50:54.275 --> 00:50:56.040
out of everything
that we got sent.


00:50:56.175 --> 00:50:57.914
I know you already said no,


00:50:58.049 --> 00:51:02.016
but can I please sing it
at the Wiltern tomorrow?


00:51:02.151 --> 00:51:04.446
I mean, it's your
concert, your tour.


00:51:04.582 --> 00:51:06.813
You should sing
whatever song you want.


00:51:07.558 --> 00:51:08.991
Okay. Yeah, just...


00:51:09.126 --> 00:51:11.990
I feel like between
managers and stylists


00:51:12.125 --> 00:51:14.229
and execs and label people,


00:51:14.365 --> 00:51:18.168
I feel like I never get a
say in anything that goes on.


00:51:18.303 --> 00:51:19.303
Right?


00:51:19.565 --> 00:51:23.236
Right, because old
people never listen.


00:51:24.039 --> 00:51:26.443
I mean, people like you think...


00:51:26.578 --> 00:51:27.734
I think people like me


00:51:27.870 --> 00:51:29.127
think people like
you don't know any...


00:51:29.210 --> 00:51:31.341
-You know what I mean.
-Yeah.


00:51:31.477 --> 00:51:33.613
I have control over my own life.


00:51:34.349 --> 00:51:36.380
Absolute control.
Photoshoot's back on.


00:51:36.515 --> 00:51:38.586
Photoshoot is back
on, grasshoppers.


00:51:38.721 --> 00:51:40.018
Chop, chop, chop.


00:51:40.154 --> 00:51:42.759
Let's make some fierce photos


00:51:42.895 --> 00:51:45.190
of this fierce girl right here.


00:51:45.325 --> 00:51:47.025
Bruh, having a job
is really hard.


00:51:47.161 --> 00:51:49.032
-Wait.
-What? "Wait" what?


00:51:49.167 --> 00:51:53.236
If your mum wrote that
song about that Jake...


00:51:53.371 --> 00:51:54.698
Yeah.


00:51:54.834 --> 00:51:56.453
...that's how we can get our
parents to split up forever.


00:51:56.536 --> 00:51:59.938
So if she is with him,
she can't marry my dad.


00:52:00.074 --> 00:52:01.439
Well, how do we find him?


00:52:03.279 --> 00:52:05.880
[Tess] It's like a
database of old people.


00:52:06.282 --> 00:52:08.684
-Jake. Yes.
-That's him from the photo.


00:52:08.820 --> 00:52:10.415
[Tess] Wait, wait, wait, look.


00:52:11.313 --> 00:52:12.250
[Tess] Okay.


00:52:12.386 --> 00:52:14.089
And he owns the Record Parlour.


00:52:14.224 --> 00:52:17.189
[Tess] He has liked
all your mum's posts.


00:52:17.325 --> 00:52:20.024
He is proper obsessed with her.


00:52:20.160 --> 00:52:22.189
Single. Okay, let's do it.


00:52:22.324 --> 00:52:23.895
Let's do it.


00:52:24.365 --> 00:52:26.629
But first, your
mum must look fit


00:52:26.764 --> 00:52:28.835
if she's gonna run into
the love of her life.


00:52:28.971 --> 00:52:30.403
And I need to change, too.


00:52:30.538 --> 00:52:34.174
Ella's stylist has pulled
the most gorgeous garms


00:52:34.309 --> 00:52:35.601
I've ever seen in
my entire life.


00:52:35.737 --> 00:52:36.945
[Ella] Do we love this for me?


00:52:37.081 --> 00:52:38.296
Girl, the label
loves this for you.


00:52:38.379 --> 00:52:39.782
-Can we just put it on your...
-No.


00:52:39.917 --> 00:52:41.037
-Maybe on your shoulder?
-No.


00:52:41.147 --> 00:52:42.747
Rest it on your head?


00:52:42.883 --> 00:52:45.152
[Tess] <i>Please, can we just
put our differences aside</i>


00:52:45.287 --> 00:52:47.923
so that I can live
my dream? Please.


00:52:48.059 --> 00:52:49.891
This is only
because of the plan.


00:52:50.026 --> 00:52:51.819
-Oh, thank you.
-You're welcome.


00:52:53.262 --> 00:52:55.695
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.


00:52:56.598 --> 00:52:59.365
[♪ "Super Graphic Ultra
Modern Girl" playing]


00:53:06.105 --> 00:53:07.673
It's not very me.


00:53:08.175 --> 00:53:10.575
Harper. This is so exciting.


00:53:10.710 --> 00:53:12.979
So, posing for the camera,
it's very different.


00:53:13.115 --> 00:53:14.982
Find a shape and then hold it.


00:53:15.117 --> 00:53:16.877
-Yeah. Okay.
-Good luck.


00:53:19.748 --> 00:53:21.486
-Where did the fruit go?
-I'm s...


00:53:26.895 --> 00:53:28.195
Oh, this is cool.


00:53:28.331 --> 00:53:30.033
-Oh, that is chic.
-It's recycled I think.


00:53:30.966 --> 00:53:31.798
'Cause I'm a pop star.


00:53:31.934 --> 00:53:33.102
-Pop out.
-Yeah.


00:53:33.570 --> 00:53:34.570
Pop.


00:53:35.034 --> 00:53:36.270
No! No! No! No!


00:53:37.641 --> 00:53:39.438
No, no, no.


00:53:39.907 --> 00:53:41.077
[in unison] Oh.


00:53:50.046 --> 00:53:52.055
[Ella] <i>Tess, your
styling is so on point.</i>


00:53:52.190 --> 00:53:54.521
You two are the coolest
adults I have ever met.


00:53:54.657 --> 00:53:55.657
Thanks.


00:53:55.784 --> 00:53:56.993
-Bye.
-[Tess] Thank you.


00:53:57.128 --> 00:53:58.820
-My mom does have a cool job.
-Yes.


00:54:02.430 --> 00:54:03.929
Think she's our new best friend?


00:54:04.065 --> 00:54:06.698
I think so. I think so.


00:54:07.101 --> 00:54:08.461
Do you guys need a ride?


00:54:08.897 --> 00:54:10.902
-Oh, yes. Totally. Yes.
-OMG, yes.


00:54:11.037 --> 00:54:12.600
[PA chimes]


00:54:12.735 --> 00:54:14.310
[Waldman] <i>Attention, students.</i>


00:54:14.446 --> 00:54:15.921
<i>You'll be happy to know
that my anaphylactic shock</i>


00:54:16.004 --> 00:54:18.114
<i>-has subsided.</i>
-[retches]


00:54:19.474 --> 00:54:20.474
[retches]


00:54:20.880 --> 00:54:23.779
-[Waldman] <i>Yes. I didn't die.</i>
-[Mr. Bates snoring]


00:54:24.886 --> 00:54:26.078
Thank you.


00:54:26.514 --> 00:54:27.589
[retches]


00:54:27.724 --> 00:54:29.115
[PA chimes]


00:54:29.250 --> 00:54:31.051
[Waldman] <i>And I hope
those who were involved</i>


00:54:31.186 --> 00:54:33.921
<i>in that food fight
are loving detention.</i>


00:54:39.560 --> 00:54:41.236
[fans cheering]


00:54:44.674 --> 00:54:45.900
Oh, no.


00:54:47.143 --> 00:54:49.443
They've gone completely rogue.


00:54:49.845 --> 00:54:50.947
[Tess] Whoo!


00:54:51.082 --> 00:54:53.674
-Yeah!
-[Tess] <i>This is so cool!</i>


00:54:53.809 --> 00:54:55.380
[Lily] What are we wearing?


00:54:55.515 --> 00:54:57.544
They're on a joyride with Ella.


00:54:57.679 --> 00:54:59.186
We'll never find them.


00:54:59.322 --> 00:55:03.357
No, but we can find Madame Jen.


00:55:07.362 --> 00:55:09.429
Are you thinking
what I'm thinking?


00:55:10.492 --> 00:55:11.530
Oh, yeah.


00:55:12.894 --> 00:55:14.803
[♪ "Spice Up Your Life" plays]


00:55:14.938 --> 00:55:16.455
-♪<i> Every boy and every girl</i> ♪
-♪<i> Spice up your life</i> ♪


00:55:16.538 --> 00:55:18.336
[Lily] Madame Jen said
she lost her table


00:55:18.471 --> 00:55:20.234
at the Larchmont Farmers Market,


00:55:20.369 --> 00:55:22.495
but now she can be seen at the
Starbucks across the street


00:55:22.578 --> 00:55:25.808
from the Larchmont Village
wine and cheese shop.


00:55:28.153 --> 00:55:29.552
Look, I know we
don't have time...


00:55:29.687 --> 00:55:30.945
But we are here.


00:55:31.080 --> 00:55:33.223
And my metabolism is
the speed of sound.


00:55:33.358 --> 00:55:35.915
-♪<i> Spice up your life</i> ♪
-[vocalizing]


00:55:36.050 --> 00:55:37.892
[Harper] I got
extra whipped cream!


00:55:38.027 --> 00:55:40.186
[Lily] My knees work!


00:55:40.322 --> 00:55:42.961
I haven't had real dairy
since Bush was president.


00:55:43.096 --> 00:55:44.360
Curly fries!


00:55:44.495 --> 00:55:45.928
[Harper] Flexibility!


00:55:46.063 --> 00:55:47.836
♪ <i>If ya know That
you feel fine</i> ♪


00:55:47.972 --> 00:55:49.566
-Mmm.
-[laughs]


00:55:49.702 --> 00:55:52.033
We really need to
find Madame Jen.


00:55:52.168 --> 00:55:55.911
Yes, but they have onion
rings on their burgers.


00:55:56.347 --> 00:55:59.044
I haven't digested
like this in decades!


00:55:59.180 --> 00:56:01.074
I'm still not full!


00:56:01.685 --> 00:56:02.845
Sugar.


00:56:03.446 --> 00:56:04.779
Remember sugar?


00:56:04.915 --> 00:56:06.680
But after this,
back to the mission.


00:56:06.816 --> 00:56:08.314
Mmm. It has my full attention.


00:56:08.450 --> 00:56:12.395
All you have to do is go in
there and flirt with Jake,


00:56:12.531 --> 00:56:15.098
and remind him why he fancied
you when you were young.


00:56:15.233 --> 00:56:16.657
Wait, I wasn't me
when I was young.


00:56:16.793 --> 00:56:18.358
And I don't know how to flirt.


00:56:18.493 --> 00:56:20.487
And I definitely don't know
how to flirt as an old person.


00:56:20.570 --> 00:56:23.531
What do they do, talk
about transitional lenses?


00:56:23.667 --> 00:56:25.868
Home repairs? John Mayer?


00:56:26.003 --> 00:56:27.700
-I... I don't know.
-Oh! I have an idea.


00:56:27.836 --> 00:56:29.745
We both wear our AirPods.


00:56:29.881 --> 00:56:31.004
That way you can help me


00:56:31.139 --> 00:56:32.398
because you have a
French boyfriend.


00:56:32.481 --> 00:56:34.382
So you definitely
know how to flirt.


00:56:35.545 --> 00:56:38.210
Yeah... Defo. Yes.


00:56:38.346 --> 00:56:40.226
I'm gonna go in, and then
I'll give you the word


00:56:40.349 --> 00:56:42.757
when to come in and make
your sexy grand entrance.


00:56:43.527 --> 00:56:45.521
What sexy grand entrance?
What do you mean?


00:56:45.656 --> 00:56:46.673
[Tess] You have to be sexy.


00:56:46.756 --> 00:56:47.956
-How?
-[Tess] Like...


00:56:49.425 --> 00:56:50.464
Sexy.


00:56:51.199 --> 00:56:52.393
I'm not doing that.


00:56:52.528 --> 00:56:54.831
[engine roaring]


00:56:59.109 --> 00:57:01.707
-[engine revs]
-Oh.


00:57:02.343 --> 00:57:04.072
♪ <i>Oh, my God</i> ♪


00:57:04.207 --> 00:57:06.849
♪ <i>Take me back The
way that I was</i> ♪


00:57:06.985 --> 00:57:09.816
♪ <i>Oh, my God</i> ♪


00:57:09.952 --> 00:57:12.519
♪ <i>You know I only tried
to Play your games</i> ♪


00:57:12.655 --> 00:57:15.285
♪ <i>So you cannot Forget my name</i> ♪


00:57:15.420 --> 00:57:20.093
♪ <i>You and I are not the same
You always had it easy</i> ♪


00:57:20.229 --> 00:57:22.057
♪ <i>Oh, my God</i> ♪


00:57:22.192 --> 00:57:25.199
♪ <i>Take me back The
way that I was</i> ♪


00:57:25.334 --> 00:57:27.802
♪ <i>The way that I was</i> ♪


00:57:27.937 --> 00:57:29.437
[chuckles]


00:57:32.370 --> 00:57:33.408
[Jake] Hey!


00:57:36.139 --> 00:57:38.646
-This is a different look.
-Yeah. Uh-huh.


00:57:38.782 --> 00:57:41.207
It's awesome. I didn't know
you were coming by today.


00:57:41.342 --> 00:57:43.214
-I got the stuff in the back.
-What stuff?


00:57:43.349 --> 00:57:44.349
What do you mean?


00:57:44.687 --> 00:57:46.856
[Tess] <i>That's him.
That's her bloke.</i>


00:57:46.991 --> 00:57:48.390
<i>What's happening?</i>


00:57:49.192 --> 00:57:50.855
He's going to get me stuff.


00:57:50.991 --> 00:57:53.822
What is your mother doing
behind my father's back?


00:57:53.957 --> 00:57:56.693
-[shushes]
-No. Hey, hey, hey!


00:57:56.828 --> 00:57:58.324
-Do not shush me. Okay?
-Get down.


00:57:58.459 --> 00:58:00.367
-He can't hear me.
-Get down. I'm ignoring you.


00:58:00.502 --> 00:58:02.371
Hey, thanks again
for doing this.


00:58:02.506 --> 00:58:06.770
What exactly are we
doing here? [chuckles]


00:58:06.906 --> 00:58:08.643
Signing the merch for
the charity auction.


00:58:08.779 --> 00:58:10.011
Oh.


00:58:10.147 --> 00:58:12.041
-Right.
-Here you go.


00:58:12.543 --> 00:58:15.483
Right. The merch.


00:58:16.612 --> 00:58:17.612
[Tess] Oh!


00:58:21.090 --> 00:58:22.557
I have a question.


00:58:23.226 --> 00:58:24.617
Do you ever think about me?


00:58:24.752 --> 00:58:26.260
About us?


00:58:26.729 --> 00:58:29.097
I'm not sure there's a right
answer to this question.


00:58:29.232 --> 00:58:35.338
I mean, do you ever miss us?


00:58:37.034 --> 00:58:39.166
You're getting
married this weekend.


00:58:39.844 --> 00:58:43.071
Unless I'm not.


00:58:43.907 --> 00:58:45.438
["...Baby One More Time" plays]


00:58:45.573 --> 00:58:47.543
[Tess] <i>Okay, very good.
Now, do something cheeky.</i>


00:58:47.678 --> 00:58:49.319
Like, flip your hair.


00:58:50.283 --> 00:58:51.520
<i>Good.</i>


00:58:51.656 --> 00:58:54.115
<i>Ooh, good. Big, big,
big moves. Big moves.</i>


00:58:54.251 --> 00:58:56.649
<i>One more. Shake
your head. Shake it.</i>


00:58:57.418 --> 00:58:59.753
<i>More. Like, all the way around.</i>


00:58:59.889 --> 00:59:01.155
<i>There you go. Shake it.</i>


00:59:02.098 --> 00:59:03.498
<i>Excellent.</i>


00:59:03.634 --> 00:59:06.669
<i>Okay, um, wink at him.
Try winking. Wink.</i>


00:59:06.804 --> 00:59:07.860
Wink.


00:59:07.996 --> 00:59:10.234
<i>Wink. One eye. One eye.</i>


00:59:10.369 --> 00:59:11.497
Now do both.


00:59:11.999 --> 00:59:14.905
<i>Wink. Okay, good.</i>


00:59:17.182 --> 00:59:19.276
Okay. Um, that's not working.


00:59:19.411 --> 00:59:20.841
Um... Uh... Oh!


00:59:20.977 --> 00:59:23.276
Bite your lip. Bite your lip.


00:59:25.149 --> 00:59:27.284
<i>Why is he looking
at you like that?</i>


00:59:27.719 --> 00:59:28.882
[muffled] I'm biting my lip.


00:59:29.285 --> 00:59:31.389
No, not your top
lip. Your bottom lip.


00:59:31.524 --> 00:59:32.995
Bite your bottom lip.


00:59:33.130 --> 00:59:34.958
<i>Like that, pouty.</i>


00:59:35.726 --> 00:59:37.091
I know what this is.


00:59:37.227 --> 00:59:38.915
I've seen this before.
You're having a stroke.


00:59:38.998 --> 00:59:40.322
-Mm-mmm. No, no.
-We need to get you help.


00:59:40.405 --> 00:59:42.096
I just need to go
to the bathroom.


00:59:42.232 --> 00:59:43.624
I just... Yeah. Gotta
go to the bathroom.


00:59:43.707 --> 00:59:45.798
-Uh, it's in the back.
-All right. I'll find it.


00:59:45.933 --> 00:59:47.839
Are you sure? I...


00:59:53.184 --> 00:59:54.510
There's no merch in the...


00:59:55.113 --> 00:59:57.548
I was really bad at
that. So bad at that.


00:59:57.984 --> 01:00:00.115
How do you know your
boyfriend liked you?


01:00:00.617 --> 01:00:01.450
[stammers]


01:00:01.586 --> 01:00:02.586
You just know.


01:00:02.717 --> 01:00:03.651
Huh?


01:00:03.787 --> 01:00:05.459
How? Like, specifically.


01:00:05.594 --> 01:00:07.321
You've dated a
guy. You know this.


01:00:07.456 --> 01:00:10.125
You have experience. Tell
me. Help me out here.


01:00:12.637 --> 01:00:15.165
Harper, I... I don't
have a French boyfriend.


01:00:15.301 --> 01:00:16.329
[gasps]


01:00:17.736 --> 01:00:19.542
My entire dating experience


01:00:19.677 --> 01:00:22.171
is watching 500
hours of<i> Love Island</i>.


01:00:22.306 --> 01:00:24.539
Wait, you're, like, the most
confident person I know.


01:00:24.674 --> 01:00:26.207
It's an act.


01:00:29.744 --> 01:00:31.112
What?


01:00:31.248 --> 01:00:33.048
Well, you're not gonna
tell everyone, are you?


01:00:33.450 --> 01:00:36.419
No. I'm not like that. I
wouldn't do that. [chuckles]


01:00:36.554 --> 01:00:37.854
Okay. Thank you.


01:00:37.990 --> 01:00:39.962
Oh! You're not gonna
hug me, are you?


01:00:40.098 --> 01:00:41.530
No, I was... Just...


01:00:41.665 --> 01:00:43.490
-No, don't do that.
-Okay, it was just...


01:00:43.626 --> 01:00:45.996
All right, look, no, we should
get back out there. Right?


01:00:46.131 --> 01:00:48.561
Because, otherwise,
he'll think I'm pooping.


01:00:48.696 --> 01:00:50.482
-[Lily] There she is!
-I see her. Right by the milk.


01:00:50.565 --> 01:00:53.141
And I see your screenwriting
career taking off.


01:00:53.277 --> 01:00:55.773
If you move over to, um...


01:00:55.908 --> 01:00:58.374
-[barista] Genre?
-Genre, yes.


01:00:58.509 --> 01:00:59.378
Genre.


01:00:59.514 --> 01:01:00.514
[barista] Elevated genre?


01:01:00.643 --> 01:01:01.847
Um...


01:01:02.283 --> 01:01:03.814
No. Sorry.


01:01:03.950 --> 01:01:06.118
-[Harper] You!
-[Madame Jen] Um. Oh.


01:01:06.253 --> 01:01:07.021
Um...


01:01:07.156 --> 01:01:08.089
How can I help?


01:01:08.225 --> 01:01:11.523
Take one wild guess.


01:01:11.659 --> 01:01:13.529
Are you gonna serve me papers?


01:01:14.660 --> 01:01:16.961
We switched bodies.


01:01:17.594 --> 01:01:18.692
Oh!


01:01:18.827 --> 01:01:20.196
Oh, my gosh.


01:01:20.732 --> 01:01:22.362
It actually worked.


01:01:22.963 --> 01:01:24.601
That's amazing.


01:01:24.737 --> 01:01:26.201
It's never worked before.


01:01:26.336 --> 01:01:28.539
Um, would you guys mind
leaving me a review


01:01:28.674 --> 01:01:29.874
or, like, five stars?


01:01:30.009 --> 01:01:31.299
And just saying,
like, "Oh, my gosh!


01:01:31.382 --> 01:01:32.745
Madame Jen was so much fun..."


01:01:32.880 --> 01:01:34.320
Tell us how to switch
back right now.


01:01:34.414 --> 01:01:35.451
Okay. All right.


01:01:35.587 --> 01:01:37.586
Um, I'll consider it
if you sign up for


01:01:37.721 --> 01:01:41.581
my Reiki and financial
management package.


01:01:41.717 --> 01:01:44.894
Tell us how to switch back,
you multi-hyphenate lunatic!


01:01:45.497 --> 01:01:48.460
Oh, my gosh. I am
a multi-hyphenate.


01:01:48.595 --> 01:01:50.027
That absolutely slays.


01:01:50.162 --> 01:01:52.760
I'm supposed to get
married in two days.


01:01:52.895 --> 01:01:54.597
Right, okay. Um...


01:01:55.333 --> 01:01:58.300
All right. Well, you have
to look at the reading.


01:01:58.436 --> 01:02:02.206
-That's the only way.
-We don't know the reading.


01:02:02.875 --> 01:02:04.580
Um, what are you talking about?


01:02:04.715 --> 01:02:06.911
I said the reading
directly to you both,


01:02:07.047 --> 01:02:09.415
multiple times, in a
scary whisper voice.


01:02:09.551 --> 01:02:11.147
Because we weren't there.


01:02:11.848 --> 01:02:12.780
That wasn't...


01:02:12.915 --> 01:02:14.786
Right! Oh, right.


01:02:14.922 --> 01:02:17.184
You weren't you because
you had switched


01:02:17.320 --> 01:02:20.424
with the other women, who are...


01:02:20.559 --> 01:02:21.690
Okay, that's...


01:02:21.826 --> 01:02:23.160
And it makes sense.


01:02:23.295 --> 01:02:27.767
Um, okay. Well... [sighs]
...the reading was,


01:02:27.902 --> 01:02:29.901
"Change the hearts
you know are wrong


01:02:30.036 --> 01:02:32.938
to reach the place
where you belong."


01:02:33.073 --> 01:02:34.793
-Didn't we try that?
-I think we tried that.


01:02:34.909 --> 01:02:37.072
-We tried it.
-Okay, the problem is


01:02:37.208 --> 01:02:39.708
your hearts might
not be the only ones


01:02:39.844 --> 01:02:41.213
that need changing.


01:02:41.348 --> 01:02:42.376
So...


01:02:42.878 --> 01:02:44.712
Mmm. Cute.


01:02:44.847 --> 01:02:45.847
[chuckles]


01:02:45.982 --> 01:02:47.914
Well, our time is up.


01:02:48.450 --> 01:02:50.121
[Harper] Wait,
but... No, no, no.


01:02:50.256 --> 01:02:51.912
There's got to be something
else you can do, right?


01:02:51.995 --> 01:02:54.559
I wish I could help you,
but my shift is starting.


01:02:55.261 --> 01:02:59.299
So, what I can do for
you is get you a cortado,


01:02:59.434 --> 01:03:01.564
an Americano, a...


01:03:01.699 --> 01:03:03.299
[mumbles]


01:03:03.434 --> 01:03:06.800
...and any kind of espresso
or non-espresso drink.


01:03:06.936 --> 01:03:07.869
[phone rings]


01:03:08.004 --> 01:03:09.070
It's your dad! Shoot!


01:03:09.206 --> 01:03:10.906
[Jake] This is all new inventory


01:03:11.041 --> 01:03:12.439
that we need to get sorted.


01:03:13.745 --> 01:03:15.112
Uh, excuse me.


01:03:16.484 --> 01:03:17.785
-Tess?
-Oh!


01:03:21.019 --> 01:03:22.922
What are you doing down there?


01:03:23.919 --> 01:03:25.320
Stretching.


01:03:26.692 --> 01:03:28.895
Ah. Yeah. I...


01:03:29.398 --> 01:03:30.689
Anna didn't...


01:03:30.825 --> 01:03:32.683
She didn't tell me that you
were gonna be here today.


01:03:32.766 --> 01:03:34.032
-Oh!
-What interview?


01:03:34.167 --> 01:03:35.547
I mean, yes, I know
the interview. Now?


01:03:35.630 --> 01:03:38.269
I was just thinking
about you the other day.


01:03:38.405 --> 01:03:39.637
Really?


01:03:40.140 --> 01:03:41.556
I've been meaning to
ask you something.


01:03:41.639 --> 01:03:43.142
Sure.


01:03:43.278 --> 01:03:48.245
And, um, I don't quite know
how to broach the subject.


01:03:48.380 --> 01:03:54.422
But is, um, your husband...
Is he still with us?


01:03:54.958 --> 01:03:58.689
Yeah. I can't believe
it. I mean, he's so old.


01:03:58.824 --> 01:04:01.163
How... How old is he?


01:04:01.299 --> 01:04:03.222
We never talk about it.


01:04:03.358 --> 01:04:05.595
Somewhere between 50 and 100.


01:04:05.730 --> 01:04:07.267
[chuckles]


01:04:07.403 --> 01:04:08.562
[Tess] Really.


01:04:08.697 --> 01:04:12.739
Yeah. Yeah. But... Okay,
let me focus for a second.


01:04:12.874 --> 01:04:15.136
I'm worried about
Anna, all right?


01:04:15.271 --> 01:04:16.636
She's been being weird with me,


01:04:16.771 --> 01:04:19.879
and she keeps asking if
I ever think about her.


01:04:20.015 --> 01:04:22.715
You know, maybe she
is reconsidering.


01:04:22.850 --> 01:04:24.646
-Reconsidering?
-[Tess] Uh-huh.


01:04:24.781 --> 01:04:28.185
Three weeks ago, she told me
how in love she is with Eric.


01:04:28.321 --> 01:04:31.155
Do you know that she
wrote a song about you?


01:04:32.527 --> 01:04:33.861
-No.
-Anna!


01:04:34.891 --> 01:04:36.260
Daughter.


01:04:36.395 --> 01:04:39.494
Why don't you tell Jake
about the song you wrote?


01:04:40.030 --> 01:04:41.463
I wrote a song about us.


01:04:41.599 --> 01:04:43.253
[Tess] You know what, I'll
give you your privacy.


01:04:43.336 --> 01:04:45.365
I'm just gonna go look
for music for old people.


01:04:45.501 --> 01:04:48.243
You know, really
old, like Coldplay.


01:04:48.879 --> 01:04:50.438
It's nice to hear
you're writing again.


01:04:50.573 --> 01:04:52.708
Yeah, can you just
give me a second, bro?


01:04:52.843 --> 01:04:54.376
Just one second.


01:04:55.010 --> 01:04:56.610
Coldplay...


01:04:56.746 --> 01:04:59.015
We need to get to the
immigration interview. Now.


01:04:59.150 --> 01:05:01.089
-Okay, let's go.
-[Anna] Yeah.


01:05:01.458 --> 01:05:02.988
Oh! My legs are so weak,


01:05:03.123 --> 01:05:05.321
my knees are cracking
like walnuts.


01:05:06.527 --> 01:05:07.554
[knees pop]


01:05:09.026 --> 01:05:10.729
[breathing heavily]


01:05:10.864 --> 01:05:12.500
What is happening right now?


01:05:12.969 --> 01:05:15.495
My brain is telling
my body to stand up,


01:05:15.631 --> 01:05:18.367
but it's like shouting
into the abyss.


01:05:19.942 --> 01:05:21.637
See? I just tried
to get up again.


01:05:21.772 --> 01:05:22.841
Okay.


01:05:22.976 --> 01:05:24.541
-Help me. Help me up.
-Okay.


01:05:24.676 --> 01:05:26.226
We have to find a way to get
to the immigration interview.


01:05:26.309 --> 01:05:27.482
-[Tess] Okay.
-[Anna] Yes.


01:05:27.618 --> 01:05:30.084
Wait, I have an idea. Come on.


01:05:30.219 --> 01:05:31.872
[Jake] So, that's why Tess
and I have a special bond.


01:05:31.955 --> 01:05:35.088
Oh, Jake. Hi. Could
we borrow your car?


01:05:35.224 --> 01:05:38.920
Oh, and don't worry, we're
totally of age to drive.


01:05:39.056 --> 01:05:41.962
Anything for you, Dr. C.


01:05:44.334 --> 01:05:45.334
You ready?


01:05:46.236 --> 01:05:47.367
Hold on.


01:05:47.503 --> 01:05:49.299
[engine revs]


01:05:50.471 --> 01:05:51.566
Whoo!


01:05:52.068 --> 01:05:53.099
[inhales sharply]


01:05:53.568 --> 01:05:55.338
Oh, that's a woman
after my heart.


01:05:55.473 --> 01:05:57.978
-[laughs] I love driving!
-I don't wanna...


01:05:58.113 --> 01:06:00.209
I don't know who
taught you how to drive


01:06:00.345 --> 01:06:02.780
-but they weren't good.
-[tires squeal]


01:06:02.916 --> 01:06:05.313
[♪ pop music playing]


01:06:05.449 --> 01:06:07.620
Wrong side! Wrong
side! Wrong side!


01:06:08.189 --> 01:06:10.582
-[Tess] Okay.
-You're gonna get us killed!


01:06:10.718 --> 01:06:12.458
-[horns honking]
-[Anna] Oh, geez.


01:06:12.593 --> 01:06:13.862
[screams]


01:06:16.064 --> 01:06:17.859
Oh! I can't look. I can't look.


01:06:18.328 --> 01:06:19.762
No, no. I'm a very good driver.


01:06:19.898 --> 01:06:21.496
[Anna screams]


01:06:26.343 --> 01:06:28.371
[both screaming]


01:06:34.682 --> 01:06:36.984
That was smashing.


01:06:39.884 --> 01:06:41.516
[Anna] Whoo!


01:06:47.929 --> 01:06:49.790
-[Tess] Oh!
-[tires screech]


01:06:49.926 --> 01:06:51.033
Hi.


01:06:51.469 --> 01:06:53.665
Hi. [chuckles] Nice car.


01:06:53.800 --> 01:06:55.102
It's totally mine.


01:06:55.237 --> 01:06:57.067
-[Anna] You think he's cute.
-[Tess] I do not.


01:06:57.202 --> 01:06:58.700
-You totally do.
-Stop. I do not.


01:06:58.836 --> 01:07:00.991
-[Anna] Yes, you do. You do.
-[Tess] I do not. Shut up.


01:07:01.074 --> 01:07:01.870
[Anna] She thinks you're cute!


01:07:02.005 --> 01:07:03.005
I do not!


01:07:03.107 --> 01:07:04.039
-Yes, she does.
-I do.


01:07:04.175 --> 01:07:05.474
-She so does.
-I do.


01:07:05.876 --> 01:07:07.172
Thanks.


01:07:07.307 --> 01:07:08.510
Dr. Coleman?


01:07:09.353 --> 01:07:10.611
Oh, my gosh. Go.


01:07:11.214 --> 01:07:12.750
That's my therapist!


01:07:12.886 --> 01:07:14.716
[Anna] You nervous?


01:07:14.852 --> 01:07:17.457
[Eric] Oh, why would I be?
We're perfect for each other.


01:07:17.592 --> 01:07:18.621
You'll see.


01:07:19.057 --> 01:07:20.896
Oh, that's cryptic.


01:07:21.031 --> 01:07:22.782
-[Anna clears throat]
-[worker] Coleman/Reyes?


01:07:22.865 --> 01:07:25.263
-Ah, yes. That's us.
-Go.


01:07:26.402 --> 01:07:27.402
My love.


01:07:27.505 --> 01:07:28.505
[Anna clears throat]


01:07:28.639 --> 01:07:30.367
-So many ruffles.
-Yeah.


01:07:31.301 --> 01:07:33.304
-There we go.
-Ah.


01:07:34.543 --> 01:07:35.835
How are you?


01:07:35.970 --> 01:07:38.612
Oh, um, I was just dumped
by my fiancé, so...


01:07:38.747 --> 01:07:39.975
-You know.
-Oh, no.


01:07:40.110 --> 01:07:42.147
I... I'm so sorry.


01:07:42.283 --> 01:07:44.913
Oh, what a decent thing
to say. Thank you.


01:07:45.048 --> 01:07:45.949
Yes, of course.


01:07:46.085 --> 01:07:48.046
Are you single? [chuckles]


01:07:48.182 --> 01:07:49.485
Kidding!


01:07:50.387 --> 01:07:52.594
Um, can I see your paperwork?


01:07:52.730 --> 01:07:53.825
-Ah, yes.
-[worker] Yeah.


01:07:53.961 --> 01:07:54.961
I'm sure you're approved.


01:07:55.058 --> 01:07:56.527
Wait. Whoa.


01:07:56.662 --> 01:07:57.848
Don't you need to see if
we really know each other?


01:07:57.931 --> 01:07:59.198
I mean, usually, yeah,


01:07:59.334 --> 01:08:03.571
but he seems like such
a kind and honest man


01:08:03.706 --> 01:08:04.936
who clearly works out.


01:08:05.072 --> 01:08:06.539
-Oh.
-A lot. [chuckles]


01:08:07.008 --> 01:08:08.239
I mean you could be a gymnast.


01:08:08.375 --> 01:08:10.043
I did once qualify
to represent the UK


01:08:10.179 --> 01:08:11.656
-in pole vaulting.
-You're kidding. Really?


01:08:11.739 --> 01:08:12.981
I'd still like for us to prove


01:08:13.116 --> 01:08:15.549
that we, you know,
are marriage material.


01:08:16.085 --> 01:08:18.987
So, what's my favorite
road trip snack?


01:08:19.122 --> 01:08:21.917
Uh, 7-Eleven hot dog
dipped in blue Slurpee.


01:08:22.052 --> 01:08:23.187
Dream vacay?


01:08:23.323 --> 01:08:24.859
Taking the girls
to the Galapagos.


01:08:24.995 --> 01:08:27.194
Harper would love
the biodiversity


01:08:27.329 --> 01:08:29.369
and I think Lily could
really benefit from the dirt.


01:08:29.496 --> 01:08:32.567
Though she really just
wants to see a, uh...


01:08:32.703 --> 01:08:35.031
Komodo dragon in the wild.


01:08:35.167 --> 01:08:36.702
It's her favorite animal.


01:08:36.838 --> 01:08:38.730
These are too, too easy.


01:08:38.866 --> 01:08:40.437
You gotta hit me
with the hard stuff.


01:08:40.572 --> 01:08:44.069
What is my guilty
pleasure pump-up song?


01:08:44.205 --> 01:08:45.277
Oh.


01:08:45.412 --> 01:08:48.344
Uh, darling, I promised
to never divulge


01:08:48.480 --> 01:08:49.946
that highly-classified
information.


01:08:50.082 --> 01:08:52.048
See? He doesn't know me.


01:08:52.184 --> 01:08:53.786
-At all. See?
-Okay.


01:08:53.921 --> 01:08:55.021
We can't get married.


01:08:55.157 --> 01:08:58.290
[groans] It's...
It's Chumbawamba.


01:08:59.387 --> 01:09:00.423
She told you?


01:09:00.559 --> 01:09:02.296
Wait. "Creepy Crawling"
or "Tubthumping"?


01:09:02.432 --> 01:09:04.693
♪ <i>I get knocked down
But I get up again</i> ♪


01:09:04.828 --> 01:09:06.828
♪ <i>You're never
gonna Keep me down</i> ♪


01:09:06.964 --> 01:09:09.434
♪ <i>I get knocked down
But I get up again</i> ♪


01:09:09.569 --> 01:09:11.573
♪ <i>You're never
gonna Keep me down</i> ♪


01:09:11.708 --> 01:09:13.233
That's the one, yeah.


01:09:13.368 --> 01:09:14.634
[chuckles, sighs]


01:09:14.769 --> 01:09:17.410
♪ <i>Pissin' the night away</i> ♪


01:09:17.546 --> 01:09:18.671
Oh, wow.


01:09:18.807 --> 01:09:23.777
♪ <i>Oh, Danny Boy, Danny Boy</i> ♪


01:09:24.722 --> 01:09:25.817
♪ <i>Danny Boy</i> ♪


01:09:25.952 --> 01:09:27.253
[sniffles, groans]


01:09:27.388 --> 01:09:29.820
-Danny was my fiancé's name.
-Okay, enough.


01:09:30.423 --> 01:09:32.392
What's my deepest, darkest fear?


01:09:32.528 --> 01:09:33.528
Oh.


01:09:34.121 --> 01:09:36.560
That your love for Harper
and need to protect her


01:09:36.695 --> 01:09:39.468
will push her away rather
than bring her close.


01:09:40.071 --> 01:09:41.829
And then she'll run
away and be a surf bum


01:09:41.964 --> 01:09:43.723
and then she'll get a
dodgy tattoo of the sun


01:09:43.806 --> 01:09:45.205
around her belly button.


01:09:46.441 --> 01:09:50.645
But you're a phenomenal
mum and Harper is amazing,


01:09:50.781 --> 01:09:52.575
so that will never happen.


01:09:56.314 --> 01:09:58.586
Well, that was really sweet.


01:09:58.722 --> 01:10:00.151
I didn't know that.


01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:02.440
[worker] You know, I approve
hundreds of marriages


01:10:02.523 --> 01:10:05.225
that... [scoffs] ...probably
won't even last a year.


01:10:05.794 --> 01:10:07.293
But you two...


01:10:13.499 --> 01:10:15.895
-Thank you.
-[clears throat] Next.


01:10:18.303 --> 01:10:20.308
Well done. We got approved.


01:10:20.444 --> 01:10:21.505
Ugh.


01:10:21.640 --> 01:10:24.176
Ugh, my seafood vendor
says we canceled.


01:10:24.312 --> 01:10:25.672
-I should deal with this.
-Bet.


01:10:25.808 --> 01:10:27.579
-Yeah, my mom's almost here.
-Okay.


01:10:27.715 --> 01:10:29.716
Uh, bye.


01:10:29.852 --> 01:10:30.650
What an odd mix-up.


01:10:30.785 --> 01:10:32.952
[tires screech]


01:10:33.087 --> 01:10:35.055
Hop in, muppet. How'd it go?


01:10:35.191 --> 01:10:37.755
Your dad knows a
lot about my mom.


01:10:37.891 --> 01:10:39.910
-I think he really loves her.
-[Tess] But did you do enough


01:10:39.993 --> 01:10:41.588
to break them up?


01:10:41.723 --> 01:10:42.960
-I don't know.
-[groans]


01:10:43.096 --> 01:10:44.528
I need to clear my mind.


01:10:44.663 --> 01:10:47.631
-Can we go somewhere?
-Yes, yeah. Get in.


01:10:47.766 --> 01:10:50.398
-[Anna] Don't drive so fast.
-[Tess] Okay. Buckle up!


01:10:50.534 --> 01:10:52.537
-[engine revs]
-[Anna screams]


01:10:52.672 --> 01:10:54.325
[Harper] "Change the
hearts you know are wrong


01:10:54.408 --> 01:10:55.788
to reach the place
where you belong."


01:10:55.871 --> 01:10:57.440
What do you think
she meant by that?


01:10:57.575 --> 01:10:58.947
[Lily] I think she
made it all up,


01:10:59.083 --> 01:11:00.198
but look on the
bright side, honey,


01:11:00.281 --> 01:11:02.611
these scooters are so much fun!


01:11:02.746 --> 01:11:03.972
Why have we never
done this before?


01:11:04.055 --> 01:11:05.578
Because you already
have one fake hip


01:11:05.713 --> 01:11:07.089
and you do not need another.


01:11:07.224 --> 01:11:09.650
Very funny. I'll have
you know, in this body,


01:11:09.786 --> 01:11:12.285
I have two real hips. [screams]


01:11:12.420 --> 01:11:13.828
[laughing]


01:11:13.964 --> 01:11:16.121
-[vendor] Whoa!
-[screams]


01:11:16.824 --> 01:11:19.200
[Harper groans] Sorry. Sorry.


01:11:21.595 --> 01:11:22.830
Nothing broke!


01:11:24.433 --> 01:11:25.364
We're invincible!


01:11:25.500 --> 01:11:26.432
Bone density!


01:11:26.567 --> 01:11:28.209
I'm not exhausted!


01:11:28.678 --> 01:11:30.343
[both laughing]


01:11:31.643 --> 01:11:36.448
-Girls, get in the car.
-[phone chiming]


01:11:38.420 --> 01:11:41.123
How do kids get away
with anything anymore?


01:11:48.556 --> 01:11:50.022
[Tess screams]


01:11:56.570 --> 01:11:59.438
You know, I hated you
a little less today.


01:12:01.204 --> 01:12:03.809
I think it's hard to hate me
when I look like your gran.


01:12:03.944 --> 01:12:05.008
[chuckles]


01:12:05.144 --> 01:12:06.379
[Tess] And...


01:12:07.448 --> 01:12:10.548
I hated you a little
less today too.


01:12:15.251 --> 01:12:18.959
I just don't understand how
anyone can dislike California.


01:12:19.094 --> 01:12:20.855
It's, like, a wrong opinion.


01:12:22.265 --> 01:12:24.523
Harper, you can't
have a wrong opinion.


01:12:24.659 --> 01:12:26.331
I mean, look around.


01:12:26.466 --> 01:12:30.330
Yes. Okay, Harper, it's lovely.


01:12:30.465 --> 01:12:31.965
It's lovely.


01:12:32.533 --> 01:12:33.802
I just...


01:12:34.809 --> 01:12:36.475
[sighs]


01:12:37.176 --> 01:12:39.005
...I miss England.


01:12:45.112 --> 01:12:47.882
We can talk about
her if you want.


01:12:50.419 --> 01:12:51.490
No, thanks.


01:12:53.722 --> 01:12:55.356
I think if I talk about her,


01:12:56.158 --> 01:12:58.365
I'm giving away what
little of her I have left.


01:13:00.703 --> 01:13:01.929
Okay.


01:13:03.507 --> 01:13:08.833
And why are you so obsessed
that I like Los Angeles?


01:13:08.969 --> 01:13:10.844
-Well, I'm not.
-Yes, you are.


01:13:10.979 --> 01:13:12.180
-No.
-Yes.


01:13:12.649 --> 01:13:16.878
And look, even if I liked it
a little bit here, I mean...


01:13:20.049 --> 01:13:23.449
You... You still
don't want me around.


01:13:23.918 --> 01:13:26.594
-Obviously not.
-Obviously not.


01:13:27.631 --> 01:13:30.331
I guess it's a good thing
we're stopping this wedding.


01:13:31.668 --> 01:13:32.894
Yeah.


01:13:35.101 --> 01:13:36.302
Where are they?


01:13:36.438 --> 01:13:37.798
They're supposed
to be home by now.


01:13:37.901 --> 01:13:40.401
This is very good. A little dry.


01:13:41.203 --> 01:13:44.636
Very fruit-forward. And
by fruit, I mean grapes.


01:13:45.239 --> 01:13:47.948
Your lack of concern,
it's not working.


01:13:48.083 --> 01:13:50.010
Just stay calm, honey.


01:13:50.578 --> 01:13:51.685
Stay calm?


01:13:52.355 --> 01:13:53.711
But I've got the
rehearsal lunch,


01:13:53.847 --> 01:13:54.956
the final dress fitting,


01:13:55.092 --> 01:13:57.084
and my wedding is in 36 hours,


01:13:57.219 --> 01:13:59.221
and I'm trapped in the
body of a ninth-grader.


01:13:59.357 --> 01:14:00.693
[Anna] I did.


01:14:00.829 --> 01:14:02.416
-I told you she approved it.
-You most certainly did not.


01:14:02.499 --> 01:14:04.109
[Anna] What difference
does it make, anyway?


01:14:04.192 --> 01:14:06.026
-It's done now.
-Where on earth have you been?


01:14:07.002 --> 01:14:08.436
-Oh.
-Well.


01:14:08.572 --> 01:14:10.536
Can't two adult women come
home when they please?


01:14:10.672 --> 01:14:12.190
What do you think you're
doing driving around


01:14:12.273 --> 01:14:13.505
like that with Ella all day?


01:14:13.641 --> 01:14:15.506
Ella needs to talk
to you, by the way.


01:14:15.642 --> 01:14:17.030
You need to give
her more attention.


01:14:17.113 --> 01:14:18.412
Why am I dressed like that?


01:14:18.547 --> 01:14:20.315
I need more attention
from you sometimes.


01:14:20.451 --> 01:14:21.860
She has a lot of stuff
to talk to you about.


01:14:21.943 --> 01:14:23.208
-[shushes]
-She was crying.


01:14:23.343 --> 01:14:24.913
Okay, I don't care
about that right now.


01:14:25.048 --> 01:14:26.306
Did you make it to the
immigration interview?


01:14:26.389 --> 01:14:28.488
Yes, I did. Just,
like, chill, okay?


01:14:28.623 --> 01:14:31.326
Or do your weird breathing
stuff that you do.


01:14:31.761 --> 01:14:32.987
Chill?


01:14:34.228 --> 01:14:35.789
I am the adult here.


01:14:35.924 --> 01:14:37.866
-I'm in charge.
-[both scoff]


01:14:38.001 --> 01:14:39.268
Doesn't look like it.


01:14:39.403 --> 01:14:41.298
You just earned
yourselves a consequence.


01:14:41.434 --> 01:14:43.662
-Ooh. No.
-Oh, no.


01:14:43.798 --> 01:14:44.697
Give me your phones.


01:14:44.832 --> 01:14:45.901
-Sure.
-[Tess] No.


01:14:46.336 --> 01:14:47.674
Psych.


01:14:47.810 --> 01:14:49.689
By the way, you're the reason
this is all falling apart.


01:14:49.772 --> 01:14:51.004
[Anna] Shut up. No, I'm not.


01:14:51.140 --> 01:14:52.660
[Tess] Yes, it totally
is. And don't...


01:14:52.774 --> 01:14:54.248
Girls, this is serious.


01:14:54.383 --> 01:14:55.878
We all need to
start getting along


01:14:56.013 --> 01:14:57.638
unless we want to be
stuck like this forever.


01:14:57.721 --> 01:15:00.555
You know, you lot are getting
the better end of this deal.


01:15:00.690 --> 01:15:03.758
It's us who are gonna be
dead in, like, five years.


01:15:03.893 --> 01:15:04.826
She's 37.


01:15:04.961 --> 01:15:06.854
I'm 36 and a half!


01:15:06.990 --> 01:15:08.753
While you two were
out having fun,


01:15:08.889 --> 01:15:10.289
we found Madame Jen.


01:15:10.424 --> 01:15:12.725
And she made us buy
business cards for everyone


01:15:12.860 --> 01:15:14.126
and a Reiki ten-pack!


01:15:14.261 --> 01:15:16.663
What even is Reiki?
Huh? What is it?


01:15:16.799 --> 01:15:18.131
Stop talking about Reiki.


01:15:18.267 --> 01:15:20.132
Well, Madame Jen said
to change your hearts,


01:15:20.267 --> 01:15:21.937
so change your
freaking dang hearts.


01:15:22.072 --> 01:15:23.992
It's the only way for us
to get out of this mess.


01:15:24.107 --> 01:15:26.214
I'm switching to
red. Do you want one?


01:15:26.349 --> 01:15:28.411
You're making Mommy
very stressed!


01:15:28.547 --> 01:15:30.546
...use Reiki now! [sighs]


01:15:30.682 --> 01:15:32.286
[♪ Moody pop music plays]


01:15:32.422 --> 01:15:35.357
♪ <i>You think that I'll leave</i> ♪


01:15:36.093 --> 01:15:38.921
♪ <i>Don't worry</i> ♪


01:15:41.330 --> 01:15:44.229
♪ <i>I just keep on</i> ♪


01:15:44.365 --> 01:15:47.234
♪ <i>Coming back</i> ♪


01:15:47.670 --> 01:15:52.933
♪ <i>I'm your good
And I'm your bad</i> ♪


01:15:53.068 --> 01:15:57.138
♪ <i>'Cause you're my baby</i> ♪


01:15:57.273 --> 01:16:02.578
♪ <i>Ooh, oh 'Cause
you're my baby</i> ♪


01:16:02.713 --> 01:16:06.047
♪ <i>Baby Baby</i> ♪


01:16:16.389 --> 01:16:20.067
[Eric] Okay,<i> Blue
Crush.</i> Look at you.


01:16:20.203 --> 01:16:22.536
Shredding the waves, dude.


01:16:22.671 --> 01:16:25.106
-Never use those words again.
-[chuckles]


01:16:25.242 --> 01:16:27.402
Wait, what are you doing here?


01:16:27.537 --> 01:16:28.839
Our lessons.


01:16:30.145 --> 01:16:31.472
What lessons?


01:16:31.608 --> 01:16:32.777
Surf lessons.


01:16:33.811 --> 01:16:34.995
But it looks like you're ready


01:16:35.078 --> 01:16:36.815
to surprise Harper
and take her out.


01:16:36.950 --> 01:16:39.788
Oh, yeah. That's really
gonna surprise Harper.


01:16:40.257 --> 01:16:41.653
-Obviously.
-[chuckles]


01:16:41.788 --> 01:16:43.990
Oh, no, I just ate
a bowl of onions.


01:16:44.126 --> 01:16:45.452
In the water?


01:16:45.921 --> 01:16:47.154
Yeah, they keep me alert.


01:16:47.821 --> 01:16:49.123
[chuckles]


01:16:49.657 --> 01:16:50.960
Okay.


01:16:52.895 --> 01:16:56.600
Look, I know it feels like


01:16:56.735 --> 01:16:59.339
we're in an
impossible situation.


01:16:59.874 --> 01:17:03.302
Maybe that's why things
have felt a bit off with us.


01:17:04.079 --> 01:17:05.546
Yeah, probably.


01:17:06.115 --> 01:17:08.846
Yeah, but Anna...


01:17:10.749 --> 01:17:14.885
I think we should stay in LA.


01:17:16.685 --> 01:17:17.921
What about Lily?


01:17:19.959 --> 01:17:22.023
Going back to London,
to Pembridge Hall,


01:17:22.159 --> 01:17:23.788
it's not going to
bring back her mum.


01:17:24.558 --> 01:17:28.264
And there's no one
keeping us there anymore.


01:17:28.900 --> 01:17:31.906
If I'm honest,
we've felt so lost.


01:17:32.609 --> 01:17:35.076
So what she needs is
to be with family.


01:17:35.712 --> 01:17:39.976
A gran like Tess, a sister
like Harper, and you.


01:17:43.548 --> 01:17:45.454
[sighs, chuckles]


01:17:46.880 --> 01:17:48.018
What is it?


01:17:48.420 --> 01:17:49.451
It's just...


01:17:50.254 --> 01:17:53.895
I can't believe how much
you love me and my family.


01:17:54.631 --> 01:17:58.857
It's a real, true love.
It's just... It's crazy.


01:17:59.427 --> 01:18:02.329
Okay. Well, you made
it look so easy.


01:18:02.865 --> 01:18:04.099
I'm gonna give it a go.


01:18:04.768 --> 01:18:05.967
I don't know if that's...


01:18:06.103 --> 01:18:07.463
Maybe I've improved
as much as you!


01:18:09.539 --> 01:18:10.539
[groans]


01:18:10.639 --> 01:18:11.639
Oh!


01:18:11.741 --> 01:18:13.405
I'm okay! [groans]


01:18:13.884 --> 01:18:15.110
Oh.


01:18:16.814 --> 01:18:18.243
[Eric] No. I'm gonna wait.


01:18:18.378 --> 01:18:20.249
I'm gonna wait for
the instructor.


01:18:20.752 --> 01:18:22.181
I mean, you were amazing.


01:18:22.317 --> 01:18:23.917
You were, like,
weaving and dodging,


01:18:24.053 --> 01:18:25.784
and you're like a pro surfer.


01:18:26.420 --> 01:18:28.553
-I'm glad we talked.
-Yeah, me too.


01:18:29.556 --> 01:18:31.157
[Eric] It's good we
came to a decision.


01:18:31.292 --> 01:18:32.859
[Anna] Yeah, dude. Really good.


01:18:33.395 --> 01:18:34.932
[Eric] See you at
the rehearsal lunch!


01:18:35.067 --> 01:18:37.539
[Anna] Totally, but my
mom said I have to...


01:18:40.840 --> 01:18:42.733
It fits perfectly.
Anna, come look.


01:18:42.869 --> 01:18:44.374
Oh, wow.


01:18:44.509 --> 01:18:45.543
[clears throat]


01:18:46.012 --> 01:18:50.310
Sweetheart... [sniffles]
...fix your posture.


01:18:51.088 --> 01:18:52.312
This is weird.


01:18:53.147 --> 01:18:55.056
Weirder for me, trust me.


01:18:55.192 --> 01:18:56.314
Really? Are you the one


01:18:56.450 --> 01:18:58.089
wearing your mom's
wedding dress?


01:18:58.225 --> 01:19:00.821
Well, I never thought I'd
get to have this experience.


01:19:00.956 --> 01:19:02.330
Especially like this.


01:19:02.999 --> 01:19:05.600
[Anna] Well, Mom, you know how
much I love to wear a dress.


01:19:05.735 --> 01:19:08.494
[Harper] Ugh. Sorry this
is such a mess, Harper.


01:19:08.630 --> 01:19:11.232
[Anna] Mom, there's
something I need to tell you.


01:19:16.604 --> 01:19:19.271
What were you talking to
my dad about this morning?


01:19:19.407 --> 01:19:22.375
Oh, we were just
talking about the lunch.


01:19:23.143 --> 01:19:24.448
What about the lunch?


01:19:24.583 --> 01:19:25.884
Just lunch stuff.


01:19:29.919 --> 01:19:32.752
Oh, right. The lunch.


01:19:32.887 --> 01:19:34.123
[Anna chuckles]


01:19:34.955 --> 01:19:37.159
Okay. Um.


01:19:38.195 --> 01:19:40.331
I'm just gonna
make a quick call.


01:19:40.466 --> 01:19:41.397
[Anna] Okay.


01:19:41.532 --> 01:19:42.571
Okay.


01:19:45.199 --> 01:19:47.906
[♪ Dramatic music plays]


01:19:57.847 --> 01:20:01.083
Oh, hi! It's Tess.


01:20:01.219 --> 01:20:05.419
Um, listen, last minute
but Anna was wondering


01:20:05.554 --> 01:20:09.095
if you might like to attend
her rehearsal luncheon.


01:20:10.132 --> 01:20:13.565
No, no. You would not be an
imposition. You know what?


01:20:13.701 --> 01:20:14.966
I think your appearance there


01:20:15.101 --> 01:20:17.265
would make it a much
more lively affair.


01:20:20.638 --> 01:20:23.637
[Eric] <i>So, I just wanted to
say that I'm very excited.</i>


01:20:23.773 --> 01:20:26.506
<i>And being at my new restaurant
makes it all the more special</i>


01:20:26.641 --> 01:20:29.144
for all of us to finally
come together as a family.


01:20:29.279 --> 01:20:32.384
So with that said,
welcome to Lily's.


01:20:32.520 --> 01:20:33.452
[guest] Congratulations.


01:20:33.587 --> 01:20:34.721
Thank you for coming.


01:20:34.856 --> 01:20:36.234
Really, Eric and I
so appreciate it.


01:20:36.317 --> 01:20:37.615
-[server clears throat]
-Oh.


01:20:38.118 --> 01:20:39.353
Right. Thanks.


01:20:40.595 --> 01:20:41.675
[server] Champagne, ladies?


01:20:41.796 --> 01:20:42.836
-Yes, please.
-Yes, please.


01:20:42.962 --> 01:20:44.426
-'Cause we're adults.
-Mm-hmm.


01:20:44.562 --> 01:20:47.260
Girls, Eric's parents are
here so best behavior, please.


01:20:47.396 --> 01:20:49.199
Stand up straight. Good posture.


01:20:49.335 --> 01:20:54.474
Anna, my soon-to-be daughter.
My heart is so full.


01:20:54.609 --> 01:20:56.139
[Anna] That's me. [chuckles]


01:20:56.742 --> 01:20:58.208
How was your flight?


01:20:58.343 --> 01:21:01.214
Oh, it was 13 hours and 30
minutes from Manila. Ugh.


01:21:01.350 --> 01:21:02.242
Major jet lag.


01:21:02.377 --> 01:21:04.142
-Some worse than others.
-[snoring]


01:21:04.278 --> 01:21:07.786
But I really love it here.


01:21:07.921 --> 01:21:09.281
Maybe Harper can
teach me the surf.


01:21:09.386 --> 01:21:12.023
-Sure, dude.
-<i> Mano po, Lola</i>.


01:21:13.158 --> 01:21:15.961
You're so silly. Only
Lily calls me Lola.


01:21:16.097 --> 01:21:18.726
But I want to support
your Tagalog learning.


01:21:18.861 --> 01:21:20.299
Keep it up.


01:21:20.435 --> 01:21:21.627
Come on, Anna.


01:21:21.762 --> 01:21:23.284
-Let's have a drink.
-No, no, no, no. We just...


01:21:23.367 --> 01:21:24.887
We have to wait for
the surprise guest.


01:21:25.233 --> 01:21:26.470
What are you talking about?


01:21:26.606 --> 01:21:28.039
Oh, just wait.


01:21:28.174 --> 01:21:31.369
-Hello, sir. Welcome.
-Ah, no, thank you.


01:21:31.505 --> 01:21:33.343
-I'm here to see someone.
-Jake?


01:21:33.879 --> 01:21:35.041
[server 2] Just alone or...


01:21:35.176 --> 01:21:36.509
What's he doing here?


01:21:36.645 --> 01:21:38.167
I invited him but I
didn't think he'd come.


01:21:38.250 --> 01:21:40.046
But, you know, he
really likes your gran.


01:21:40.182 --> 01:21:41.479
My mom's gonna freak out,


01:21:41.615 --> 01:21:43.106
-you know that?
-I know. So will my dad.


01:21:43.189 --> 01:21:45.724
-That was the whole point.
-[groans] You...


01:21:45.859 --> 01:21:49.930
Dr. C. Thank you
for inviting me.


01:21:50.065 --> 01:21:52.727
I... I saved your number.
I hope that's okay.


01:21:52.862 --> 01:21:54.562
Of course.


01:21:55.131 --> 01:21:56.463
-Hi, there.
-Hey.


01:21:56.599 --> 01:21:58.632
Hmm. I think I'm gonna
have to ask you to leave.


01:21:58.768 --> 01:22:00.436
Uh, now?


01:22:00.572 --> 01:22:03.776
But, uh, you know, your mom,
she really wanted me here.


01:22:03.911 --> 01:22:06.913
Right. I'm sure.
[chuckles] Well...


01:22:08.383 --> 01:22:10.481
[whispers]


01:22:10.616 --> 01:22:11.645
[Anna] Okay.


01:22:12.382 --> 01:22:14.052
-I got you.
-Thank you so much.


01:22:14.188 --> 01:22:15.904
-[Tess] No, no, no. Wait.
-You're the best, bro.


01:22:15.987 --> 01:22:16.919
-Wait!
-Thank goodness.


01:22:17.054 --> 01:22:18.320
[Jake] I will be right back.


01:22:18.456 --> 01:22:20.142
-[Tess] No. Jake, don't go.
-Ah, Tess. Tess.


01:22:20.225 --> 01:22:21.892
-Yes?
-Uh, can we have a chat later?


01:22:22.027 --> 01:22:23.589
-It's regarding Lily.
-Oh!


01:22:23.724 --> 01:22:26.093
If it's regarding Lily,
we should chat now.


01:22:26.228 --> 01:22:27.394
[Harry] My big sister, Anna.


01:22:27.530 --> 01:22:30.068
After every atomic
wedgie you gave me,


01:22:30.204 --> 01:22:33.200
I always knew that you
also had an atomic heart.


01:22:33.335 --> 01:22:34.809
-Cheers.
-[guests] Cheers!


01:22:34.945 --> 01:22:38.142
Anna and I decided we
should all stay in LA.


01:22:39.677 --> 01:22:40.446
What?


01:22:40.582 --> 01:22:42.117
-Yes.
-What?


01:22:42.252 --> 01:22:42.977
Everyone?


01:22:43.113 --> 01:22:44.713
-Yes.
-[Tess stammers]


01:22:44.848 --> 01:22:45.950
As a therapist,


01:22:46.085 --> 01:22:47.547
I was hoping to
get your thoughts


01:22:47.682 --> 01:22:49.549
on the best way to
approach it with Lily.


01:22:51.686 --> 01:22:53.593
But, I know how you feel
about billable hours


01:22:53.728 --> 01:22:55.692
so we can chat later. Yeah?


01:22:55.827 --> 01:22:57.056
[Tess] Okay. Okay.


01:22:57.192 --> 01:22:58.932
[breathing heavily]


01:23:05.568 --> 01:23:09.269
You bloody backstabber.
I know what you did.


01:23:09.404 --> 01:23:10.443
-Shh!
-[Harry] All right,


01:23:10.579 --> 01:23:11.712
who wants to speak next?


01:23:11.848 --> 01:23:13.244
Father of the groom looks ready.


01:23:13.379 --> 01:23:15.543
No, no. I have a few
choice words for the bride.


01:23:15.678 --> 01:23:17.558
-I would like to make a toast.
-[glass clinking]


01:23:17.650 --> 01:23:18.785
That's crystal.


01:23:18.921 --> 01:23:20.213
Uh, we have a toasting triangle.


01:23:20.348 --> 01:23:21.885
-Oh, piss off.
-Okay.


01:23:22.521 --> 01:23:25.253
I would like to make a
toast to your future husband


01:23:25.388 --> 01:23:28.627
so that he knows
what kind of woman


01:23:28.763 --> 01:23:29.995
he is getting married to.


01:23:30.130 --> 01:23:32.994
[chuckles] He does,
he does, he does.


01:23:33.130 --> 01:23:34.702
He knows who he's marrying


01:23:34.837 --> 01:23:36.267
and he can make
his own decisions


01:23:36.403 --> 01:23:39.140
and he knows not to be
manipulated by other people.


01:23:39.275 --> 01:23:40.202
Tess.


01:23:40.338 --> 01:23:42.873
Hey, gramps, this is between us.


01:23:43.009 --> 01:23:44.345
[Anna] Listen to your husband.


01:23:44.481 --> 01:23:46.439
[Tess] You listen to me.


01:23:46.575 --> 01:23:48.274
[Harper] Ugh, Ella.
What does she want?


01:23:48.710 --> 01:23:51.044
Micro cilantro from the
foothills of Oaxaca.


01:23:51.180 --> 01:23:52.686
It was not my fault.


01:23:53.088 --> 01:23:56.016
That micro cilantro is
bursting with flavor.


01:23:56.152 --> 01:23:57.319
But it is your fault


01:23:57.455 --> 01:24:00.687
that the cilantro
has no loyalty to...


01:24:00.823 --> 01:24:03.190
-[Lily] What are they doing?
-We have to stop them.


01:24:03.326 --> 01:24:04.855
Are you doing all right, Harp?


01:24:04.991 --> 01:24:07.896
[sighs] Ella, this is
the last thing I need.


01:24:08.032 --> 01:24:09.270
Oh, Jake's back already.


01:24:09.405 --> 01:24:10.405
Jake? Who?


01:24:10.500 --> 01:24:12.200
Jake, what... What
are you doing here?


01:24:12.336 --> 01:24:14.001
-Uh...
-It was all her, I swear.


01:24:14.137 --> 01:24:16.005
Hello. Um, and you are?


01:24:16.140 --> 01:24:18.011
That's Anna's ex-boyfriend.


01:24:18.146 --> 01:24:20.710
-What? Why?
-She invited her ex-boyfriend?


01:24:20.846 --> 01:24:22.048
[guests] What?


01:24:22.183 --> 01:24:23.497
Because she still
has feelings for him.


01:24:23.580 --> 01:24:25.100
-Okay. That's not... That...
-[Lily] No.


01:24:25.183 --> 01:24:26.882
-What? I...
-No. Uh...


01:24:27.018 --> 01:24:28.285
After the appetizer,


01:24:28.420 --> 01:24:30.171
Anna said she wasn't
feeling well so I went...


01:24:30.254 --> 01:24:31.993
Right. I wasn't feeling well.


01:24:32.863 --> 01:24:34.040
Okay, but not from
the food here.


01:24:34.123 --> 01:24:35.190
The food is fine.


01:24:35.325 --> 01:24:36.958
-Too fishy. No.
-It's fish.


01:24:37.094 --> 01:24:38.899
It is not the food.


01:24:39.035 --> 01:24:41.435
She's just on her
period. That's all.


01:24:41.571 --> 01:24:43.069
She's on her period.


01:24:43.936 --> 01:24:45.036
I'm on mine right now.


01:24:45.171 --> 01:24:46.371
-I got it.
-I didn't know where


01:24:46.503 --> 01:24:47.526
-you are in your cycle...
-I know, dude.


01:24:47.609 --> 01:24:48.743
It's fine. Thanks.


01:24:48.879 --> 01:24:50.127
Can someone please explain to me


01:24:50.210 --> 01:24:51.591
-what's going on here.
-I don't know.


01:24:51.674 --> 01:24:53.411
-Let's just tell the truth.
-Don't let her.


01:24:53.547 --> 01:24:56.012
She shouldn't explain anything
because she will just lie.


01:24:56.147 --> 01:24:57.551
-Hey, me?
-She lies.


01:24:57.686 --> 01:24:59.548
-Yeah.
-I trusted you.


01:24:59.683 --> 01:25:02.318
I know, but you don't
know what he said to me.


01:25:02.454 --> 01:25:04.391
You weren't there.
You didn't hear it.


01:25:05.193 --> 01:25:07.491
I don't think this
marriage should happen.


01:25:07.627 --> 01:25:10.359
Well, you know what? It's
not just about what you want.


01:25:10.495 --> 01:25:12.135
It's about what she
wants and she wants...


01:25:12.232 --> 01:25:13.512
It isn't ever about what I want.


01:25:13.629 --> 01:25:15.359
-It's always about you.
-That's enough.


01:25:15.495 --> 01:25:16.602
Does everyone want this?


01:25:16.738 --> 01:25:17.738
Okay, that's enough.


01:25:17.872 --> 01:25:19.038
Well, yes. Some of them do.


01:25:19.174 --> 01:25:20.832
-[dishes clatter]
-Hey, that's enough!


01:25:24.837 --> 01:25:27.075
The girls fighting is one thing


01:25:27.210 --> 01:25:28.516
but this is your mum.


01:25:29.152 --> 01:25:31.986
And for some reason, your
ex-boyfriend is here.


01:25:32.949 --> 01:25:33.750
Yeah.


01:25:33.885 --> 01:25:36.316
Anna, I love you


01:25:36.719 --> 01:25:39.422
but you're clearly
having second thoughts.


01:25:41.558 --> 01:25:43.889
This isn't working
for our families,


01:25:44.024 --> 01:25:47.100
and we always said we'd
put our families first.


01:25:47.964 --> 01:25:49.201
So...


01:25:52.641 --> 01:25:53.865
We can't do this.


01:25:56.105 --> 01:25:57.575
I can't do this.


01:25:57.710 --> 01:25:58.776
[sobs]


01:25:59.745 --> 01:26:03.116
Lily, help your grandparents.
I'll meet you at the valet.


01:26:03.817 --> 01:26:05.052
The wedding's off.


01:26:06.516 --> 01:26:08.847
[crying] He's right. It's over.


01:26:09.448 --> 01:26:10.486
[Anna] Wait, no.


01:26:11.619 --> 01:26:12.741
Wait, please, please, please.


01:26:12.824 --> 01:26:13.626
No.


01:26:13.762 --> 01:26:14.994
I'm so sorry. I promise,


01:26:15.130 --> 01:26:16.888
I didn't mean for
this to happen.


01:26:18.900 --> 01:26:20.265
[whispers] I think you did.


01:26:25.771 --> 01:26:26.702
Well.


01:26:26.838 --> 01:26:28.801
[crying]


01:26:30.245 --> 01:26:33.476
-I guess we did it.
-Yeah. [chuckles]


01:26:40.489 --> 01:26:41.416
Uh...


01:26:41.552 --> 01:26:43.185
I know this isn't the best time


01:26:43.320 --> 01:26:45.721
but can I have my car back?


01:26:45.857 --> 01:26:47.160
[scoffs]


01:26:51.457 --> 01:26:52.858
Maybe later.


01:26:55.100 --> 01:26:57.104
[emotional music plays]


01:27:05.514 --> 01:27:06.575
[sighs]


01:27:11.344 --> 01:27:12.383
Mom!


01:27:15.052 --> 01:27:16.520
She seems upset.


01:27:17.223 --> 01:27:19.192
No, she just needs some space.


01:27:23.264 --> 01:27:26.399
What about you?
Are you doing okay?


01:27:26.935 --> 01:27:29.037
Oh, yeah. I'm always okay.


01:27:30.830 --> 01:27:32.898
It would be fair if you weren't.


01:27:33.667 --> 01:27:36.374
That all got pretty crazy.


01:27:39.210 --> 01:27:40.676
I worry what will happen


01:27:40.811 --> 01:27:43.975
when Tess doesn't have those
two to drive her crazy.


01:27:45.921 --> 01:27:47.880
You're worried about her?


01:27:50.853 --> 01:27:52.855
I'm worried Tess
would be really lonely


01:27:53.358 --> 01:27:55.252
if all of you moved to London.


01:27:55.388 --> 01:27:56.823
[sighs]


01:27:57.624 --> 01:27:59.496
You're a good guy, Ryan.


01:28:01.595 --> 01:28:03.401
Thank you. [chuckles]


01:28:04.298 --> 01:28:05.598
Go on.


01:28:05.733 --> 01:28:07.834
Maybe this isn't for me to fix.


01:28:10.579 --> 01:28:11.805
[sighs]


01:28:15.785 --> 01:28:17.415
Mind if I join you?


01:28:18.346 --> 01:28:19.417
[sniffles]


01:28:20.856 --> 01:28:22.849
-Okay.
-Okay.


01:28:24.923 --> 01:28:26.226
[sighs]


01:28:26.927 --> 01:28:28.195
Are you okay?


01:28:31.123 --> 01:28:33.398
I haven't seen my
dad that upset...


01:28:36.167 --> 01:28:37.798
since my mum died.


01:28:41.569 --> 01:28:43.111
And it was all my fault.


01:28:45.237 --> 01:28:49.843
You know, when Ryan
asked me to marry him,


01:28:51.480 --> 01:28:52.912
I thought a lot about


01:28:53.047 --> 01:28:55.255
what Anna and Harry's
dad would have said.


01:28:57.259 --> 01:28:59.083
How he would have felt about it.


01:29:00.326 --> 01:29:02.955
I think he'd be so happy for us.


01:29:04.499 --> 01:29:08.702
That we found someone
who loved us all so much.


01:29:08.837 --> 01:29:10.435
[breathes shakily]


01:29:18.940 --> 01:29:20.613
I think my mum would
feel the same way.


01:29:20.748 --> 01:29:21.945
Yeah.


01:29:22.915 --> 01:29:27.120
-[sobs] I really miss her.
-[cries] I know. It's okay.


01:29:27.256 --> 01:29:28.989
She would be so
disappointed in me.


01:29:29.124 --> 01:29:31.256
-No, no, no.
-Yes, she would.


01:29:31.391 --> 01:29:34.527
Because I was very
selfish. I was.


01:29:34.663 --> 01:29:35.554
No.


01:29:35.689 --> 01:29:38.496
I was, and I know it.


01:29:39.331 --> 01:29:44.029
No, she'd know your heart.


01:29:44.839 --> 01:29:46.097
[sniffles]


01:29:47.536 --> 01:29:48.943
I just... I should...


01:29:49.078 --> 01:29:51.069
-Find my dad...
-[Lily] Yeah.


01:29:52.178 --> 01:29:53.907
...and... and apologize.


01:30:01.984 --> 01:30:04.758
[audience chanting]
<i>Ella, Ella, Ella.</i>


01:30:04.893 --> 01:30:07.387
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:07.522 --> 01:30:09.928
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:10.063 --> 01:30:12.833
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:13.202 --> 01:30:15.595
[Anna] Why are you
walking so fast?


01:30:15.730 --> 01:30:17.129
I can't walk as fast as you.


01:30:17.264 --> 01:30:19.048
[Harper] Ella keeps texting
me the word "urgent,"


01:30:19.131 --> 01:30:20.567
and her show starts, like, now.


01:30:20.702 --> 01:30:21.782
[Anna] But what about Eric?


01:30:21.904 --> 01:30:23.233
I think we should go back, Mom.


01:30:23.369 --> 01:30:24.722
I thought there was a way
to make everyone happy


01:30:24.805 --> 01:30:26.071
but there's not, all right?


01:30:26.207 --> 01:30:27.631
But I think that we
should go back for Eric.


01:30:27.714 --> 01:30:30.278
-I really should...
-Come on. My client needs me.


01:30:30.413 --> 01:30:31.609
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:31.744 --> 01:30:34.481
Ella, Ella, Ella.


01:30:34.617 --> 01:30:36.620
[♪ Pop music plays]


01:30:37.423 --> 01:30:38.652
♪ <i>You're my confidant</i> ♪


01:30:38.787 --> 01:30:39.819
♪ <i>You're my underdog</i> ♪


01:30:39.954 --> 01:30:41.095
♪ <i>You're the one I want</i> ♪


01:30:41.231 --> 01:30:42.694
♪ <i>'Til it's said and done</i> ♪


01:30:42.829 --> 01:30:44.498
♪ <i>Call it delicate
All the benefits</i> ♪


01:30:44.633 --> 01:30:46.366
♪ <i>Invisible string
When we separate</i> ♪


01:30:48.663 --> 01:30:51.028
Don't go! Stop the car!


01:30:51.163 --> 01:30:53.701
-Tess?
-Don't go! Stop the engine!


01:30:53.837 --> 01:30:56.335
I'm not. The
engine's not even on.


01:30:56.471 --> 01:30:58.973
♪ <i>You hold it down When
I'm lost and found</i> ♪


01:30:59.109 --> 01:31:01.142
♪ <i>Look in my eyes
Be so profound</i> ♪


01:31:01.278 --> 01:31:03.144
♪ <i>Don't need to say a
thing We lose or win</i> ♪


01:31:03.279 --> 01:31:05.677
♪ <i>Together, you and
me We got everything</i> ♪


01:31:05.813 --> 01:31:08.520
♪ <i>One fine day</i> ♪


01:31:08.656 --> 01:31:10.951
♪ <i>Yeah We're going
there anyway</i> ♪


01:31:11.086 --> 01:31:14.092
-[Athena] Ella, he loves you!
-I love you!


01:31:14.228 --> 01:31:17.562
♪ <i>One fine day</i> ♪


01:31:18.925 --> 01:31:20.097
Cely, is everything okay?


01:31:20.233 --> 01:31:21.525
Yeah, everything's fine.


01:31:21.660 --> 01:31:22.703
Okay.


01:31:23.339 --> 01:31:24.995
I wonder what the
big emergency was.


01:31:25.130 --> 01:31:27.405
♪ <i>Happier happy days</i> ♪


01:31:27.541 --> 01:31:29.402
♪ <i>Right where I do belong</i> ♪


01:31:29.537 --> 01:31:30.542
Surprise!


01:31:31.145 --> 01:31:32.412
What are you doing here?


01:31:32.547 --> 01:31:33.897
Ella said you said
you missed performing.


01:31:33.980 --> 01:31:35.105
I...


01:31:35.241 --> 01:31:36.113
And that you told
her she could do


01:31:36.249 --> 01:31:37.249
any song she wanted to.


01:31:38.182 --> 01:31:39.476
You did?


01:31:39.612 --> 01:31:41.674
Dressing room is right around
the corner. Put this on.


01:31:41.757 --> 01:31:42.949
Why?


01:31:43.084 --> 01:31:44.370
Well, because we're
not 15 anymore.


01:31:44.453 --> 01:31:45.290
Dolphins.


01:31:45.425 --> 01:31:46.853
-Get in there. Okay.
-What?


01:31:46.989 --> 01:31:48.271
-Let me know when she's ready.
-Crazy.


01:31:48.354 --> 01:31:49.543
I can't believe you're
making me do this.


01:31:49.626 --> 01:31:50.955
Don't make fun of my dress.


